{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting","id":776169,"title":"Exalted fans have contradictory desires for and ideas about Lunar shapeshifting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-28T13:12:39-08:00","id":776169,"title":"Exalted fans have contradictory desires for and ideas about Lunar shapeshifting","content":"<b>I've seen this a lot. Some people argue that the default method of Heart's Blood Hunting is too bloody and murderous and combat-oriented, and other people argue that Changing Moons should absolutely keep the same disguise-oriented anima effect they've always had. I'm pretty sure these arguments even come from the SAME people, though never at the same time.<br /> <br /> Well, it's time to put these two impulses up face-to-face and show the contradictions between and underneath them.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;We Don't Want To Be Animals.&quot;</b><br /> In part, the desire for the Changing Moons to keep their disguise power is a blind reaction against the aversion to the basic Heart's Blood Hunt. It lets the player avoid the combat and the killing and the blood. It lets them play <i>X-Men</i>'s Mystique or Morph, especially if they ignore the character's totem and spirit shape and pick a Tell that isn't an animal feature.<br /> <br /> Let me say upfront that I don't condemn this sort of character build. I myself argue for the existence of Lunar disguise Charms on par with Alchemical disguise Charms (save for a Tell which the Lunar perhaps can't so easily suppress as the Alchemical can disguise her clay-like flesh and Soulgem), which would make this sort of character build available to Lunars of any Caste, not just Changing Moons. But more on that <i><b>later</b></i>.<br /> <br /> However, while I applaud exploring <i>characters</i> who want to avoid their more beastly aspects out of distaste or self-loathing, I think that <i>players</i> who want to avoid animal associations are making a mistake if they choose to play Lunar Exalted. At least half of the drama inherent to the concept of the self-hating Lunar is that the Lunar must eventually confront that side of herself -- even consistently choosing to reject it means being confronted by it on a <i>recurring</i> basis. Is that really what the <i>player</i> wants out of the character?<br /> <br /> Certainly, the Exigent book is going to be released before the next Lunars manual, and the developers have made sure to include the Chosen of Masks, a woman who can look like other people without any bent towards animals. Far more like Mystique. Even right now in the corebook, Solars have disguise Charms so thorough that they're practically person-to-person shapeshifting, without any need to hunt, and the Socialize Charms let you create alternate personae with their own, different strengths and talents. Choices like this let a player avoid hunting and killing and blood entirely, without having to cut off entire limbs from the Exalt's splat and Charmset.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;We Love Animals, But <i>Must</i> We Be Red In Tooth And Claw?&quot;</b><br /> But there are people who very much love Lunar animal associations and wish to embrace them while still keeping the default Hunt at arm's length. There are two different but often inclusive reasons for this: (1) the player doesn't want to play a murderer, or perhaps wants to play a vegetarian who is horrified by the idea of eating meat or drinking hot arterial blood, or (2) the player simply wants to play a socially-specialized Changing Moon and doesn't want to invest into combat capability.<br /> <br /> Again, let me say upfront that I applaud these character concepts! Even further, I don't think trying to play a vegetarian Lunar is missing the point of the splat, though it still touches in a positive way upon the drama of rejecting the path of least resistance and most reward (or at least, the quicker reward).<br /> <br /> I certainly want non-lethal methods of Heart's Blood Hunting to return as paths of mastery that provide bloodless alternatives. And yes, not just having sex with the target, for the same reason that the writers included the Red Rule. Not every player or gaming group is comfortable with bringing sex into the gaming session, and this should be respected.<br /> <br /> But some people have taken the argument that if non-lethal methods are going to be allowed at all, why can't killing be a matter of choice? In fact, why not stick the killing method on those brutish Full Moons as a Caste feature, and let us social Changing Moons have the more humane option, and us clever No Moons have the more intellectual option?<br /> <br /> There are multiple reasons why.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>First</i>, this goes back to the reason why anyone should be playing a Lunar Exalted in the first place. Even the least combat-oriented Changing Moon or No Moon can turn into a bear, or an elephant, or a shark, or any beast with considerable muscle and killing power, without the least bit of Ability or Background or Charm investment in combat. True, not all of these Lunars <i>will</i>, but ANY of them <i>can</i>. Additionally, Third Edition has lowered the bar on the minimum level of combat investment required to kick ass in a fight, or at the very least to survive and flee a fight gone bad. A bear or shark or elephant often has the advantage in running away from a losing situation -- they're not just large, they're fast!<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Second</i>, Second Edition screwed up the Hunt. No, I'm not talking about the minimum length of time needed to hunt something, nor the Willpower cost, nor the inability to take and store Heart's Blood you couldn't yet use. I mean, all of those things sucked, but there was a much <i>bigger</i> mistake. Second Edition emphasized the image of a single Lunar hunting alone, personally chasing a beast down, and killing it in mortal combat. Obviously, Full Moons have the advantage in this specific range of scenarios, and other concepts get the shaft.<br /> <br /> But First Edition had a much more open, flexible, and forgiving emphasis. It insisted only that the Lunar be the one to strike the killing blow and taste the hot life's blood. It explicitly mentioned that several other characters could participate in the hunt, which naturally meant that the Lunar who takes the Heart's Blood didn't need to participate beyond marking off the final health level.<br /> <br /> Naturally, Full Moons would often be able to take any Heart's Blood they wanted personally and without help, but excelling in physical situations is why players choose Full Moons to begin with. Naturally, Changing Moons and No Moons would have to either rely on their Full Moon party member to help them with killing something, or else they would need to use their social powers to persuade NPCs to corner and cripple the beast for them, or else they would have to construct traps or cast spells to get the job done... <i>and using methods like those are exactly why players chose to play Changing Moons and No Moons in the first place.</i> The game was working as intended, and it can work that way again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Third</i>, if killing something and taking its blood becomes no easier than any other method, it loses its dramatic power. Making it the most basic way for all Lunar Exalted to steal the forms of others presents a moral dilemma for those characters concepts which would care about such a moral dilemma at all. How can you have a social or intellectual Lunar who struggles to reject her beastly side if by default she has a bloodless way to steal forms? How can your pacifist Full Moon have a moral victory unless there's a temptation to reject?<br /> <br /> This is also why there should never be a Hunt that involves merely beating someone unconscious to take their form. That's just an objectively more convenient form of the default method. It would be like an upgrade to Blazing Solar Bolt that lets you use the Charm without spending the Willpower cost and without needing to substitute any other cost in its place; why would you ever spend the Willpower cost again? The choice becomes meaningless.<br /> <br /> It's not like killing the target in the basic Hunt was ever an advantage compared to a KO. Sure, you could eat the body to dispose of the evidence, or toss it off a cliff, but you could also do the same to a victim you'd beaten unconscious; it's not like they could fight back. This alternative method is thus just a pure upgrade that kills one of the most interesting conflicts of the hunt without introducing another conflict to take its place.<br /> <br /> Now, let me say upfront that I am <i>eagerly</i> hoping for a Charm that lets you challenge someone to a contest of some kind to steal their shape without killing them; that would allow you to beat someone unconscious in a martial arts duel and take their face while leaving them alive. But that's different from the carte blanche to ambush someone in a dark alley at night. Unlike the basic Hunt or the proposed &quot;Hunt without killing&quot;, THIS kind of hunt requires you to warn your target that you want to confront them, gives them the option of rejecting your challenge, and might even give them the option of choosing the specific form or place of the contest. Which offers a completely different set of advantages and disadvantages to the basic hunt in a way that &quot;just beat them unconscious&quot; does not.<br /> <br /> <br /> To answer the question of this section, &quot;No, you don't <i>have</i> to be 'red in tooth and claw' to be a Lunar. But that doesn't mean it should be just as easy. Abyssals face similar problems with avoiding incidental killing of people they don't even want to kill, and Sidereals face problems with wearing as much armor as they might like or finding as much starmetal as they would need, and Alchemicals have this Clarity business as well as the limitations of their physical Charms. All splats face challenges that reinforce their core themes and which lend weight to their decisions.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Why Bother Making Disguise Into A Charm?</b><br /> Okay, now it is <i><b>later</b></i>. Let's return to the conflict between the people who want to keep the old Changing Moon anima power, and the people who want to see that turned into a Charm.<br /> <br /> I've already addressed most of the reasons why people are adverse to this proposed change. There are certainly other arguments as well.<br /> <br /> For instance, Changing Moon players don't want to spend a Charm investment on something they've been able to take for granted. However, not every Changing Moon concept involves wearing other people's faces; Changing Moons can be entirely centered around training and commanding beasts and men in battle, or the ever-popular Pretty Kitty Revolution. To cover all three of these Changing Moon concepts equally, it would make sense to give the Caste a new anima ability that enhances their social persuasion (and intimidation) abilities in much the same way that the Full Moon anima effects enhance their athletic prowess. Which means one less social Attribute Charm that a face-stealing Lunar has to buy, which offsets the cost of needing to buy one disguise Charm.<br /> <br /> However, the most frequent and heart-felt argument is that wearing other people's faces is somehow more appropriate and useful to Changing Moons than it is to Full Moons and No Moons. This is also the most BASELESS argument I've ever heard on the matter.<br /> <br /> No Moons can benefit very much from looking exactly like the owner of a library when there are other scholars present; he might be able to sneak in as a mouse, but a mouse turning the pages of a book to read it is rather conspicuous! A No Moon also has much more use for using human disguises to spy upon others in a social setting and overhear their dangerous gossip and secret confessions -- a Changing Moon is persuasive enough to manipulate people without this knowledge, but using knowledge to leverage the world to their desires is what a No Moon is all about. Sharp ears and blackmail cover all sorts of shortcomings in persuasive talent.<br /> <br /> And what about Full Moon assassins? While it is a mistake to think of all assassination methods as involving direct combat and brute force rather than poisons or traps, it is a similar mistake to assume that all Full Moons must always choose to fight openly on the battlefield. The ability to assume anyone's face is an invaluable tool for getting close enough to a target for a private explosion of deadly violence, without having to defeat all of the target's army and bodyguards first.<br /> <br /> People play Lunar Exalted to be werewolves, skinwalkers, and facestealers. All Lunar Exalted are capable of becoming werewolves with a single Charm purchase. Why should one Caste have better talent at being skinwalkers and facestealers than the other two?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Disguise Charms versus Heart's Blood</b><br /> Finally, some may ask what the point of having Lunar disguise Charms for wearing other peoples faces would be, when it would seem to invalidate any point in stealing the Heart's Blood of other people.<br /> <br /> Except following this rejection to its logical conclusion would mean getting rid of the old Changing Moon anima power anyway.<br /> <br /> But it also ignores, forgets, or refuses to imagine the advantages to having a person's Heart's Blood beyond taking their face. Perhaps they were larger or stronger or more graceful than you -- the disguise Charm should not cover this. Perhaps they had a functional, physical mutation or two which you would find useful for purposes other than convincing people you have them and thus obviously are who you appear to be -- a disguise Charm should not cover this.<br /> <br /> Second Edition offered Flickering Star Infusion, for a way to keep your victim's death from being detected by most elements within Heaven and its Bureau of Destiny, by keeping the victim's thread of Destiny alive within the Loom of Fate. If Sidereals tried to ascertain the validity of your assumed identity by placing an Astrological Curse or Blessing upon your stolen name, you could bear the Curse to keep your cover, or enjoy the Blessing as much as possible. There's also receiving Infallible Messengers intended for your victim, where NOT receiving them would give you away, or where the utter failure of the spell would reveal your victim's death.<br /> <br /> There are also potential Heart's Blood Charms for taking advantage of skills the victim had which you do not. Treating your victim as a mentor for anything they knew in life, to shorten your training times, or to learn Martial Arts or Spells which would normally require lots of searching for living sifus or investigation of forbidden libraries. To say nothing of Lunar versions of the Solar personae Charms, which create personae based on the personalities and skills of the people you killed.<br /> <br /> Finally, the option to steal Heart's Blood without killing anyone opens up SO MANY possible Charms to use against other people. Bonuses to track them down and locate them no matter where they hide. Charms to better understand them, piercing their masks and lies to see the true motivations underneath. Charms to undermine their Resolve against the hypnotic sway your social influence can exert through the bond of the blood the two of you share in your veins.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Conclusions</b><br /> So, every side of these issues I can think of come down on this:<br /> <br /> 1) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/380970-changing-moon-lunar-caste-anima-powers\">Changing Moons need a different anima power</a>, and their old anima power, in so far as it returns at all, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question\">needs to become a Charm available to all Lunar Exalted</a>.<br /> <br /> 2) The basic Heart's Blood Hunt (or at least the First Edition version) is good, and doesn't need to be fixed, replaced, or somehow made &quot;equal&quot; to other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-29-2015, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:50:28-08:00","id":776183,"title":"","content":"I disagree.<br /> <br /> There is really not a more succinct explanation on all of why I disagree, but a big part of it is that a lot of people (not necessarily you) want to play shapeshifters, look at Lunars, and want them to be any kind of shapeshifters just because they can shift shape. But Lunars aren't merely the shapeshifter Exalted -- they are Lunars, and trying to play a non-Lunar with them, even one who does shapeshift, will end up in disappointment, whatever Lunars end up as in this edition. Trying to make Lunars less &quot;Lunar&quot; just because there are shapeshifting concepts not covered by them is to do them a disservice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:57:09-08:00","id":776184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776183#post776183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree.<br /> <br /> There is really not a more succinct explanation on all of why I disagree, but a big part of it is that a lot of people (not necessarily you) want to play shapeshifters, look at Lunars, and want them to be any kind of shapeshifters just because they can shift shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is you saying that I am wrong, while agreeing with one of the statements I made and not actually refuting anything I said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Lunars aren't merely the shapeshifter Exalted -- they are Lunars, and trying to play a non-Lunar with them, even one who does shapeshift, will end up in disappointment, whatever Lunars end up as in this edition. Trying to make Lunars less &quot;Lunar&quot; just because there are shapeshifting concepts not covered by them is to do them a disservice. </div> </div> </div>Is this you agreeing with many of the points I made, as though you wish to support my post rather than reject it.<br /> <br /> <br /> In short, I have no idea what you are arguing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:06:26-08:00","id":776193,"title":"","content":"I cannot refute such a long post bit by bit, but the problem is more fundamental than what the post is saying, so much as what the post is about. This isn't just a Lunar thing. It also showed up a lot in Second Edition, when Sidereals were &quot;the martial artist Exalted&quot;, and Abyssals were &quot;the Exalted of the dead&quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem is not so much what you are saying, so much as the topic itself. In many cases I've seen, Exalted fans rarely have contradictory ideas about Lunar shapeshifting. They have ideas about shapeshifting in general, and these contradict with Lunars. At that point I am far more inclined to ignore those ideas in favor of what the Lunars are, instead of trying to reconcile the two.<br /> <br /> ((Sorry, this is not me being snippy at you specifically, just thistopic of argument and what I presume brought you to make this post.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:14:29-08:00","id":776198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776193#post776193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot refute such a long post bit by bit, but the problem is more fundamental than what the post is saying, so much as what the post is about. This isn't just a Lunar thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In so far as it informs people's stances on the Changing Moon anima power, the idea of turning that anima power into a Charm, and the exact form that the Heart's Blood Hunt should take, it is very much a Lunar thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> You may be right in that some parts of the underlying assumptions in the player-base touch upon more than just the Lunar Exalted, but those are not my focus. I'm not arguing about them, and you aren't actually refuting my conclusions.<br /> <br /> So it's not accurate to say you disagree, which sounds like you disagree with my conclusions, rather than with the idea that this is an isolated problem. Because I never argued that this is an isolated problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> If my thread gives you a way to springboard off and create another thread to discuss the wider implications which bother you, good. But why did you come into my thread to argue about those, in such a way that it looks at first glance like you're rejecting everything I said, when I was concerned with something more specific to the Lunar Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-28-2015, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:22:35-08:00","id":776202,"title":"","content":"I really don't want my Lunar shapeshifting to be the same thing as when a solar learns Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise only with a silver-for-gold palette swap, because that was basically what 99% of lunar material was in 2e. If a player really wants to play a lunar with bloodless shape changing and refuses to play a solar with larceny, they can learn sorcery and convert Disguise of the New Face into 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:33:30-08:00","id":776209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776202#post776202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't want my Lunar shapeshifting to be the same thing as when a solar learns Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise only with a silver-for-gold palette swap, because that was basically what 99% of lunar material was in 2e. If a player really wants to play a lunar with bloodless shape changing and refuses to play a solar with larceny, they can learn sorcery and convert Disguise of the New Face into 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for the Lunar, it's not Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise, because the effects can be quite permanent and much more thorough.<br /> <br /> In First Edition, Shaping the Ideal Form let the Lunar make permanent changes to her true human form, altering her size, coloration, and even physical gender. Anything but the Tell was fair game, and there was no seeing through the disguise (other than recognizing the Tell) because it wasn't technically a disguise. There was no true appearance underneath, because the new appearance was true. All without committing any motes or using any props.<br /> <br /> From there, it's not a stretch at all to alter your appearance to look exactly like some other specific person, but because you're still working from your true shape, your Tell is very much visible and needs to be disguised somehow, which is not a thing a Solar needs to worry about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, are you rejecting Courtesan's Possession; ie: the sex-as-hunt Charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T15:17:21-08:00","id":776233,"title":"","content":"How is Shaping the Ideal Form meaningfully different than just a sliver-hued Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise/Perfect Mirror with the minor flaw of being unable to change the Tell? If that's what you think Lunar shapechanging-as-disguise should be, how is the Lunar different than a Solar who can sometimes turn into an werewolf when he fights?<br /> <br /> I don't reject Courtesan's Possession as a concept. I've never seen it in play where the person who took it wasn't playing &quot;First Age Ma-Ha-Suchi reborn!&quot; or worse, a lunar rapist concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:34:00-08:00","id":776298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776233#post776233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Shaping the Ideal Form meaningfully different than just a sliver-hued Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise/Perfect Mirror with the minor flaw of being unable to change the Tell? If that's what you think Lunar shapechanging-as-disguise should be, how is the Lunar different than a Solar who can sometimes turn into an werewolf when he fights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disguise is more than just one Charm. Combat is more than just one Charm. I think minor differences here and there combine with major differences elsewhere and snowball into a completely different kind of experience.<br /> <br /> But if we have to agree to disagree on the question of whether every single pair of vaguely related Charms must be completely different across two splats, then I'm okay with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't reject Courtesan's Possession as a concept. I've never seen it in play where the person who took it wasn't playing &quot;First Age Ma-Ha-Suchi reborn!&quot; or worse, a lunar rapist concept. </div> </div> </div>My sympathies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T19:14:47-08:00","id":776367,"title":"","content":"My Lunar has Courtesan's Possession. He got the form of his girlfriend, and the form of his Solar Mate, when he slept with a Raksha who another Lunar had turned into the form of his Solar Mate; her husband, so she got that form through Courtesan's Possession.<br /> Those are all the forms he has. He's got Temperance 3 (we haven't converted over yet), he's not keen on sleeping with loads of people to get their form.<br /> <br /> Anyway. I agree with pretty much everything in the OP.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, in the game I run there was a vegetarian Lunar, an Immaculate Monk (heretical of course). He only turned into one form (an elephant). Later, as the other party members influenced him away from the Immaculate Philosophy, he gained a handful of forms, but not very many.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T19:18:41-08:00","id":776368,"title":"","content":"I foresee two strongly possible outcomes to 3e Lunars.<br /> <br /> Either they are widely reviled because they don't fit everyone's perfect vision of what a Lunar is (something that is literally impossible)<br /> <br /> Or they're universally panned because &quot;eh, they're okay, I guess. I liked my version better.&quot;<br /> <br /> Either way, I'd consider it a personal favor it we could put a hold to all Lunar conversation until we have something we can actually talk about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T19:28:57-08:00","id":776371,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't really know what I want from Lunars. As long as they have animal-themes, and barbarian-themes (ie are not completely different thematically from before) that's okay.<br /> Basically, I want somethi\u200bng to inspire me, the way I wanted new fluff to inspire me (but obviously didn't know what new fluff I wanted per-se, if you see what I mean).<br /> I've been playing a Lunar for like 4 years, I'm kind of bored of them.<br /> <br /> So, basically, I just want something exciting, well-written, and semi-new!<br /> <br /> I do like what I've seen so far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T19:44:11-08:00","id":776379,"title":"","content":"I do have this bit of constructiveness to say. I really enjoyed the two page spread on Lunars in the 3e book, as well as the bits that were conveyed in the antagonist section. I'm eager to see how Lunars pan out in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T05:28:37-08:00","id":776524,"title":"","content":"Re: overlapping Lunar and Solar mechanics which this thread touched on, Lunars are a specific thing, and I would think they should get mechanics which most simply implement that thing, not guided by any sort of &quot;Well, the way that makes sense to implement this would be as Solars do it.... but we can't have them do it the way Solars do it, so here's this sort of weird and arbitrarily restricted way of doing it which no one actually wants, just so we can say it's different&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think you have to trust in a combination of the paths being through attributes rather than abilities, and the Charms being rooted in transformation into animal forms (of sorts - including beastmen and others who are animalish but not exactly any real animal), and the different natures of Luna and the Unconquered Sun (and Maidens, etc.) to naturally differentiate Lunars vs others, combined with solid execution. This seems like the &quot;No single Charm from splat X should overlap another single Charm from splat Y&quot; thing again.<br /> <br /> My feeling on Lunars is that really I want this solidly executed, through all three Castes, plus a strong emphasis on the Lunars as transforming and animalistic heroes with many selves who perform great deeds and who grow in their different selves through their deeds: rediscovering and fixing ancient magical treasure, protecting people under their command, slaying and taming mighty Raksha and oppressive gods, exploring Wyld kingdoms and the far parts of Creation no one can reach through supernatural animal and animalistic forms that can go further than man, bringing Luna's justice and enlightenment to unjust places and times, building peace between and a better future for peoples at war. At the same time, I want them to have the greater than human flaws expected of Exalted and generate interesting drama- petty jealousy, anger, hubris and arrogance, rivalry, harsh and unbending moralism, impractical excesses of compassion, hunger for power, indecision.<br /> <br /> I don't really care too much about the concept of playing out guerilla warfare vs the Realm (a la Maoist / Islamist / separatist rebels, etc), really, or the internal politics of guerilla war insurrection. Nor about playing a person who eats people and animals to steal their form and face. That's just my take!<br /> <br /> So it'll be interesting to see what the Lunars actually offer here, and also what the Lunars' fanbase actually wants in regards of these different elements. What would people actually prefer to see the Lunars do? Not assuming that guerrilla warfare and hunting and stealing forms versus what I guess I would label heroic fantasy drama are mutually exclusive or in contradiction, but there's a balance, and a question of emphasis, here.<br /> <br /> For Lunars generally, on your post StG, although I think you're smart enough to know this already, and the implication may already be there, I think there's a big gap between both a vegetarian character and a character who wishes to avoid murder generally, and players wanting to play a character who can murder, but for human reasons, not connected with hunting, of a literal or metaphorical sort. I don't know how much support there should be among Lunars for characters who are not interested in being a hunter of any sort. I personally am not so interested in assuming forms by hunting and the stealing of forms, so much as find assuming animal forms as a pathway for enabling mighty heroism to be an interesting concept to explore.<br /> <br /> (StG, sorry if this post is not too heavy on responses to much of what you said, although it is around 2,500 words long and seems like quite a complicated argument... 200-300 words or less summary version?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T09:35:58-08:00","id":776633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776524#post776524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: overlapping Lunar and Solar mechanics which this thread touched on, Lunars are a specific thing, and I would think they should get mechanics which most simply implement that thing, not guided by any sort of &quot;Well, the way that makes sense to implement this would be as Solars do it.... but we can't have them do it the way Solars do it, so here's this sort of weird and arbitrarily restricted way of doing it which no one actually wants, just so we can say it's different&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think you have to trust in a combination of the paths being through attributes rather than abilities, and the Charms being rooted in transformation into animal forms (of sorts - including beastmen and others who are animalish but not exactly any real animal), and the different natures of Luna and the Unconquered Sun (and Maidens, etc.) to naturally differentiate Lunars vs others, combined with solid execution. This seems like the &quot;No single Charm from splat X should overlap another single Charm from splat Y&quot; thing again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I feel.<br /> <br /> A lot of Alchemical Charm effects worked exactly like Solar Charm effects, but there were so many other differences in their other effects and in how their Charms worked on a basic level that they still came off as very unique.<br /> <br /> More unique than the Lunar Exalted would be, but that's because no other Exalted relates to their Charms the way the Alchemicals do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't really care too much about the concept of playing out guerilla warfare vs the Realm (a la Maoist / Islamist / separatist rebels, etc), really, or the internal politics of guerilla war insurrection. Nor about playing a person who eats people and animals to steal their form and face. That's just my take! </div> </div> </div>I'm personally hoping for support for those characters who want to bloodlessly prey upon people to steal their forms, if only to use the Heart's Blood of those victims against them later in various &quot;sympathetic magic&quot; ways. Especially when the Lunar would find killing these people virtually impossible. Lunars should be able to change the rules of the game and come at problems from new angles.<br /> <br /> But I am certain that there will be room to tell Lunar stories which don't involve the war against the Realm at all. The Threshold is a big place, and it's not impossible for Lunars, Dragon-Blooded, and Sidereals to make strange bedfellows in one particular region against a common foe.<br /> <br /> Which is the sort of story I'm personally more interested in playing. The Dragon Uncle, the Godfather of Dragons, a Lunar who wanders the Threshold looking for Lost Eggs and giving them a step up in the world which doesn't involve leaving their struggling communities or imperiled kingdoms for the empty promises of the Realm. The Threshold of Creation needs all the heroes it can get, and those heroes need all the training and connections that a Lunar (and his secret Sidereal partner) can provide.<br /> <br /> It's not that I object to the main story of the Silver Pact waging guerrilla war against the Realm, though. That absolutely should be the main story of the splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Lunars generally, on your post StG, although I think you're smart enough to know this already, and the implication may already be there, I think there's a big gap between both a vegetarian character and a character who wishes to avoid murder generally, and players wanting to play a character who can murder, but for human reasons, not connected with hunting, of a literal or metaphorical sort. </div> </div> </div>Your question is: &quot;What about characters who want to murder someone just because that person needs to die, rather than for Heart's Blood or other material or magical rewards?&quot;<br /> <br /> If it has absolutely nothing to do with Heart's Blood, then it has absolutely nothing to do with my points in this thread. Whether or not your character has the motivation and the resolve to murder people for any other reason is up to you. Nothing in the basic system of the game prevents it, and the question is no different for Lunars than any other character, save that a Lunar might be able to get Heart's Blood out of the murder as an incidental bonus if she so chooses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know how much support there should be among Lunars for characters who are not interested in being a hunter of any sort. </div> </div> </div>How broadly are you thinking of &quot;any sort&quot;?<br /> <br /> Some Lunars literally hunt in the fields, but others hunt metaphorically. They hunt in ballrooms and bedrooms, in ball-courts and law-courts, through oaths fulfilled and vows broken.<br /> <br /> In plainer language, Robert Vance wrote a Charm where a Lunar could steal your Heart's Blood by successfully suing you in a court of law; he not only takes your money, but your face. If you want to play a Lunar who seeks to bring justice to the world, this seems like a fitting method.<br /> <br /> There was Defeated Technique Mastery which allowed a Lunar to steal another splat's Charms by beating them at some mutually-agreed-upon contest. Obviously that sort of thing is hideously unbalanced, but it should have been a method of Heart's Blood acquisition from the beginning. It also doesn't need to be a martial arts duel -- it could be a footrace, a cooking contest, a children's card game, or a Rap Battle of Epic History (the Vikings called it &quot;Flyting&quot;).<br /> <br /> The corebook's Changing Moon has a way to gain forms through deals. I have envisioned a Charisma-based Charm where the Lunar sincerely swears an oath so hard, it creates in him a Major or Defining Intimacy towards the promise. With an upgrade, he can use this power to swear a mutual oath with someone, and if the Lunar fulfills the oath or if the other party breaks their side of the bargain, the Lunar magically and non-lethally gains their Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> Even without illusions of light and sound, there is plenty of room for Lunars to filter &quot;hunter&quot; into &quot;trickster who is always looking to get the better of his enemies and rivals by being clever&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (StG, sorry if this post is not too heavy on responses to much of what you said, although it is around 2,500 words long and seems like quite a complicated argument... 200-300 words or less summary version?) </div> </div> </div>Traditionally, reading the thesis at the beginning of an essay and the conclusions at the end of the essay should give you the summation.<br /> <br /> The conclusion section is clearly labeled such. The thesis is the big bolded paragraph at the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T13:30:38-08:00","id":776770,"title":"","content":"Most of your post is very agreeable (like animal focus = good)!<br /> <br /> However, I've read through the it multiple times, and I'm still not seeing an actual argument for why Full Moon's shouldn't be the ones who use the ol' heart-eating method as their default, whilst the others do not, merely some vague reasons as to why you think they might be able to have everyone use it.<br /> <br /> You seem to think the main objection is that other castes might not be able to eat hearts, and you argument is predicated on this narrow thinking. It took me a while to work out where you were coming from because it was such an odd assumption. So let's look at your reasons:<br /> <br /> First reason - Anyone can turn into a big mean animal, and it's easier to be basically okay at combat. Only relevant if you assume capability is the issue (and somewhat overstated).<br /> <br /> Second reason - Well, someone else/magic/theoretical traps for which the game has never had any rules can do it for you! Again, entirely focused on capability, and seemingly unable to see the pretty huge problem with &quot;Just get someone to do it for you!&quot; when others do not have to do that. So you've focused on capability, but even there you've fallen down - taking shapes is a core, perhaps the core Lunar ability, but you seem to think only Full Moons should be able to do it easily, reliably, and without burning Charm slots to do so. That's not very good reasoning, I would suggest.<br /> <br /> Third reason - It should be easiest for Full Moons, and harder for everyone else, because that's most dramatic! That's the start of an argument, but unfortunately that's as far as you go. You never really present good reasoning as to why everyone should have to use a method that fits one Caste perfectly, and is trivially easy for them, beyond that you like the specific, narrow, and dare I say it, repetitive drama of &quot;I have to kill this being to take it's form!&quot;, which is always going to boil down to &quot;Oh, well fuck that guy! *CHOMP*&quot; or &quot;Nope!&quot;. It's not exactly taxing or involving after literally the third or fourth time (esp. as you support alternate methods).<br /> <br /> Some of your &quot;alternative methods&quot; presented are also pretty strange, and seem focused entirely around taking forms from humans. I literally do not see a single suggestion from you for taking forms from animals. Why is this? You agree that animal forms are a big part of Lunars, but then you're all about suing or shagging or foot races or whatever for taking forms from others, none of which apply to animals (I hope! Otherwise it's all a bit Jerry Springer).<br /> <br /> Finally you focus on the difficulty issue - you claim being able to KO as well as kill is a pure upgrade. It is, of course, but you fail to recognise that the other forms could have default methods as difficulty and potentially even as disturbing as the heart-eating, and that no-one, that I'm aware of is demanding they get to simply KO people and take their faces. Obviously such a method should be a bit more involved and risky, like having to shown their own true to face to the target or something, or having to keep the target alive for say, a month or a year after they last use his form, or else they suffer some kind of curse/backlash (which would make you think pretty hard about whether to use it or not on a lot of people or creatures).<br /> <br /> Thankfully you avoid the obvious nonsense of the vampire feeding comparison.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, you present nothing beyond opinion as to why we shouldn't have three castes with three different <i>default</i> methods of taking forms (esp. if they can expand them later). It's pretty dull if every Lunar works exactly the same way at their core, though, and doesn't really support the Caste distinction. In fact, contrary to what you were saying, the very centrality of this issue makes a good place to distinguish the Castes, rather than to make them all the same.<br /> <br /> All that said, again, I agree with the rest of what you're saying.<br /> <br /> Oh except one thing from a later post - Hunter is not Trickster. One does not fit into the other. They are very different archetypes, and when you mix them together, you weaken both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","user":"Eurhetemec","date":". 11-29-2015, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","name":"Eurhetemec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T17:06:46-08:00","id":776888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eurhetemec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776770#post776770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I've read through the it multiple times, and I'm still not seeing an actual argument for why Full Moon's shouldn't be the ones who use the ol' heart-eating method as their default, whilst the others do not, merely some vague reasons as to why you think they might be able to have everyone use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, has anyone offered a <i>strong</i> reason why Changing Moons and No Moons should <i>not</i> have the basic Hunt, or why either of them should have a different basic Hunt?<br /> <br /> How about this argument? Heart's Blood is named thus for a reason, and that reason is that all Lunars must start from the place of consuming arterial blood from the creatures they kill. If other, non-bloody methods were just as natural to half or two-thirds of the Lunar Exalted Host, the name wouldn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to think the main objection is that other castes might not be able to eat hearts </div> </div> </div>Not Castes. Builds. A Changing Moon and No Moon can easily be built with plenty of combat capability... but many players who choose those Castes, and especially those who choose to play Changing Moons, will not WANT to invest their characters traits into combat ability, and may thus feel like the basic Hunt is unfair.<br /> <br /> I've heard Changing Moon players complain, not that they CAN'T hunt and kill beasts, but that they don't WANT to have to hunt and kill beasts. They don't want to have to buy Charms in order to have other, bloodless methods of Hunting, because that is a Charm they cannot invest into social or mental prowess.<br /> <br /> It would also be a Charm that a Full Moon can't invest into physical prowess, so the Full Moon Caste doesn't have the advantage there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First reason - Anyone can turn into a big mean animal, and it's easier to be basically okay at combat. Only relevant if you assume capability is the issue </div> </div> </div>Capability is very much an issue when Changing Moon and No Moon players think that they can't play the non-combat-oriented character concepts they want and still have the capability to hunt for Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second reason - Well, someone else/magic/theoretical traps for which the game has never had any rules can do it for you! </div> </div> </div>Third Edition has battlegroups, Backgrounds for followers and bodyguards to serve as a consistent source of allied battlegroup, a barter action to allow the exchange of money for services if you need to hire a battlegroup, and command actions for making a battlegroup stronger.<br /> <br /> Third Edition has rules for traps, as well as poison. Second Edition also had rules for traps, tucked away as they were, but would &quot;I trick the tiger into falling into a pit trap&quot; be so hard to fudge? A Survival roll against the tiger's Awareness check, and then inflict lethal falling damage.<br /> <br /> In previous Editions, storytellers should not be dicks. Is getting a bunch of professional mortal hunters to trap a tiger so that you can shoot the final arrow really so dramatically important that it needs to be a scene, or is it the sort of thing that can happen offscreen so that the rest of the gaming group can get on with dealing with the raksha, angry dead, or Dragon-Blooded?<br /> <br /> Of course, in previous Editions, false animal shapes you needed to hunt weren't really worthwhile to begin with. Form lock would prevent you from using them in combat, and Deadly Beastman Transformation was better than most any of the pitifully written-up animals included in past corebooks. In fact, their pitiful stats also meant that they weren't as much of a challenge for a group of mortal hunters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the pretty huge problem with &quot;Just get someone to do it for you!&quot; when others do not have to do that. </div> </div> </div>How is it a problem that Full Moons can generally fight much better than other Lunars? Is it a problem that Dawns are supposed to fight better than other Solars?<br /> <br /> How is it a problem that a social-oriented character -- one who is designed specifically to convince people to do stuff for the character, so that she doesn't have to do it for herself -- then has to use the powers she was designed to have in order to get people to do stuff for her so that she doesn't have to do it herself?<br /> <br /> How is it a problem that a Sorceror has to use Flight of the Brilliant Raptor to blow up his victims? Or for a Lunar crafter to build a tool or weapon or trap that he can use to make his task easier?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you've focused on capability, but even there you've fallen down - taking shapes is a core, perhaps the core Lunar ability, but you seem to think only Full Moons should be able to do it easily, reliably, and without burning Charm slots to do so. </div> </div> </div>So the Full Moon isn't &quot;burning Charm slots&quot; on his Strength damage Charms, Dexterity dodge Charms, and Stamina soak Charms?<br /> <br /> He invested to fight, so he gets to be good at fighting.<br /> <br /> For that matter, why aren't the Changing Moon and No Moon having just as easy of a time at this? Okay, so Lunar physical Charms have always been better than social and mental Charms, but that was never the way things should have been. The Changing Moon SHOULD have just as much ease with getting other people to hunt for her. The No Moon SHOULD have just as easy a time with setting up a trap or casting a wizard's fireball at the problem.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Full Moon who does the job personally and alone has to deal with the bleeding wounds he receives and the lost motes he spent. OR he can benefit just as much from being in a party as the Changing Moon and No Moon. He can hunt alongside the Changing Moon's hired help and with the weapon that the No Moon made for him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third reason - It should be easiest for Full Moons, and harder for everyone else, because that's most dramatic! </div> </div> </div>My third reason had nothing to do with Castes, and everything to do with why the basic Hunt was a good thing that shouldn't be changed or replaced for any Lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the start of an argument, but unfortunately that's as far as you go. </div> </div> </div>I had a lot of points to cover, and you may have noticed that my essay was already longer than most forumites would want to bother reading.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You never really present good reasoning as to why everyone should have to use a method that fits one Caste perfectly </div> </div> </div>Burden of proof? I don't have to argue as strongly for NOT changing something as I have to argue FOR changing something.<br /> <br /> But I would love to respond to any arguments you wish to make for what alternate methods of Hunting should be given to the Changing Moons and No Moons. I'm sure that will get my mind going.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some of your &quot;alternative methods&quot; presented are also pretty strange, and seem focused entirely around taking forms from humans. I literally do not see a single suggestion from you for taking forms from animals. Why is this? </div> </div> </div>Because very, very few people have ever complained about killing animals.<br /> <br /> However, I have for an entire year now been an advocate of a Charm that would give you the Heart's Blood of any animal whom becomes your familiar, without needing to kill or even hunt the beast. I can point you to the threads where I posted such ideas... they might even be two years old by now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you fail to recognise that the other forms could have default methods as difficulty and potentially even as disturbing as the heart-eating </div> </div> </div>The reason why the basic Heart's Blood is basic was never about the difficulty. Sometimes it's the most difficult Hunt, and sometimes it is the easiest, all depending on the Lunar, the prey, and the situation.<br /> <br /> Likewise, sometimes getting Heart's Blood through other methods is easier or more difficult. Not every Lunar is going to find sexing up a target easy, and other times a desirable target is already throwing themselves into the Lunar's bed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh except one thing from a later post - Hunter is not Trickster. One does not fit into the other. They are very different archetypes, and when you mix them together, you weaken both. </div> </div> </div>If not the trickster, then how about The Thief? Like the hunter, the thief is trying to take away something that the victim doesn't want to lose, and like the hunter, the thief often needs to be very clever about doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T21:20:31-08:00","id":776983,"title":"","content":"Given that Lunars are waaaay down the pipeline, so much that even the Antagonist section may not be entirely acurate once they come out, it's not a guaranteed thing, but looking at the Lunar Shapeshifting Trickster on page 547...<br /> &quot;In addition to taking forms by drinking the heart\u2019s blood, he has learned to temporarily steal a person\u2019s form through seduction or as repayment for a service or favor done.&quot;<br /> So, I take it, at the moment taking Heart's Blood is still the default, but you can learn other tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T23:56:23-08:00","id":777030,"title":"","content":"Looks like (though as you say, that could change).<br /> <br /> As a No Moon player*, I have no problem with my default method being to hunt down and kill an animal. I can still kill it by shooting it full of sorcery, or trap it in a spike pit, or whatever (in actuality, I tend to turn into another animal and do it). It's bestial and savage and I may be a No Moon*, but I'm still a Lunar!<br /> I wouldn't terribly mind if No Moons and Changing Moons had different default methods, as long as they were a)still evocative of monsters in some way, b)not particularly better (that knack for gaining people's forms by knocking them out? Ugh! I refuse to buy it), and c)it was still possible to learn the Full Moon way.<br /> <br /> Like, you get one Heart's Blood acquisition charm depending on your caste and you can learn others.<br /> <br /> But that's not generally how these things work.<br /> <br /> So, I think that the default method is fine, with Essence 1 charms for methods like sexual intercourse**, payment for services, or whatever, works fine. Maybe still the method of drinking other Lunar's blood to learn forms***, though there's some issues with that one.<br /> <br /> *My character is actually an ex-No Moon because he learnt Shatter the Silver Cage, but he's still a sorcerer whose charms are mostly in Perception, with very little combat ability, so basically he's a No Moon.<br /> <br /> **I do like Lunars as humans who are also bestial monsters. But as one caveat to this, I would be willing to say that this knack only works if it's consensual sexual intercourse. I'm sure the writers can think of a metaphysical reason for this (the target must on some level give of themselves, even if they don't realise they're giving their identity). I mean, I never knew anyone who was eaten by a cannibal, I have known people who've been victims of sexual assault, as I'm sure have most other players.<br /> <br /> ***This is how I learned human forms and a Tyrant Lizard form. Also, what allowed my Lunar and the other Lunar to take turns impersonating the Emperor, as we both had the same form after she ate him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-30-2015, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T05:03:18-08:00","id":777090,"title":"","content":"Too many words, so I'll try to answer briefly and maybe you can too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776888#post776888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, has anyone offered a <i>strong</i> reason why Changing Moons and No Moons should <i>not</i> have the basic Hunt, or why either of them should have a different basic Hunt?<br /> <br /> How about this argument? Heart's Blood is named thus for a reason, and that reason is that all Lunars must start from the place of consuming arterial blood from the creatures they kill. If other, non-bloody methods were just as natural to half or two-thirds of the Lunar Exalted Host, the name wouldn't make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an argument about the name, not the function, and irrelevant to what I'm saying. Obvs. if the different Castes had different abilities they'd be called different things...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776888#post776888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Capability is very much an issue when Changing Moon and No Moon players think that they can't play the non-combat-oriented character concepts they want and still have the capability to hunt for Heart's Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that they want to have the capability to gain shapeshift forms, which is distinct from the &quot;hunt for Heart's Blood&quot; deal specifically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776888#post776888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it a problem that Full Moons can generally fight much better than other Lunars? Is it a problem that Dawns are supposed to fight better than other Solars?<br /> <br /> How is it a problem that a social-oriented character -- one who is designed specifically to convince people to do stuff for the character, so that she doesn't have to do it for herself -- then has to use the powers she was designed to have in order to get people to do stuff for her so that she doesn't have to do it herself?<br /> <br /> How is it a problem that a Sorceror has to use Flight of the Brilliant Raptor to blow up his victims? Or for a Lunar crafter to build a tool or weapon or trap that he can use to make his task easier?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a problem when killing things is the easiest, fastest and most direct way to get shapeshift forms. Not sure why this is hard to understand. If all Solars had to defeat an small army to gain a new Charm or something, then, yes, it would be a problem that that Dawns were better at fighting, because gaining new Charms is something all Solars do.<br /> <br /> So when &quot;kill it and take it's heart&quot; is the default (and only non-Charm-based) way to take a form, yes it's a problem that only one Caste is so good at it they can just randomly decide to do it, and the other two have to go into elaborate, time-consuming and less effective ways of doing things. They also basically can't do it without help, and that's a problem, because Lunars are rarely played as a group of Lunars - according to OPP themselves, Lunars are usually a part of a group of other Exalts (and often the only Lunar), so they have to be designed on that basis, not on the basis that other Lunars can help them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776888#post776888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Full Moon isn't &quot;burning Charm slots&quot; on his Strength damage Charms, Dexterity dodge Charms, and Stamina soak Charms?<br /> <br /> He invested to fight, so he gets to be good at fighting.<br /> <br /> For that matter, why aren't the Changing Moon and No Moon having just as easy of a time at this? Okay, so Lunar physical Charms have always been better than social and mental Charms, but that was never the way things should have been. The Changing Moon SHOULD have just as much ease with getting other people to hunt for her. The No Moon SHOULD have just as easy a time with setting up a trap or casting a wizard's fireball at the problem.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Full Moon who does the job personally and alone has to deal with the bleeding wounds he receives and the lost motes he spent. OR he can benefit just as much from being in a party as the Changing Moon and No Moon. He can hunt alongside the Changing Moon's hired help and with the weapon that the No Moon made for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this isn't how Lunars are normally played. The &quot;all-Lunar&quot; group is a rarely-seen thing. You're also continuing to fail to understand that one Caste being way better than all the rest at something they all have to do is a problem. Essentially, you're claiming the heart-eating method should be something everyone has to consider, whilst simultaneously thinking it's fine for it to be much less viable for 2 out or 3 splats. That's very unconvincing reasoning, I'd suggest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776888#post776888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My third reason had nothing to do with Castes, and everything to do with why the basic Hunt was a good thing that shouldn't be changed or replaced for any Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and it SHOULD have considered Castes, that's the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776888#post776888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Burden of proof? I don't have to argue as strongly for NOT changing something as I have to argue FOR changing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>You accepted that burden when you demanded a return to the 1E way of doing things and suggested you were defeating the arguments of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776888#post776888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I would love to respond to any arguments you wish to make for what alternate methods of Hunting should be given to the Changing Moons and No Moons. I'm sure that will get my mind going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure it's productive to suggest alternate methods for the other Castes unless your mind is open on this subject. Your current posts suggest it's closed, and that you have made up your mind that heart-eating is mandatory for everyone as the default. If you're just going to pick holes in other ideas, not going to bother. If you can be constructive/additive/run with the ideas, great, and I will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=776888#post776888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not the trickster, then how about The Thief? Like the hunter, the thief is trying to take away something that the victim doesn't want to lose, and like the hunter, the thief often needs to be very clever about doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thief is a different archetype to Hunter as well, and in fact, mythically, the Thief and the Hunter are often at odds. Plus Trickster is the RIGHT archetype for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","name":"Eurhetemec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T08:01:33-08:00","id":777151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777030#post777030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't terribly mind if No Moons and Changing Moons had different default methods, as long as they were a)still evocative of monsters in some way, b)not particularly better (that knack for gaining people's forms by knocking them out? Ugh! I refuse to buy it), and c)it was still possible to learn the Full Moon way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. All Lunars should be able to kill for Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> But I don't see other, equally meaningful ways to gain Heart's Blood in a way that justifies keeping its name.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eurhetemec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777090#post777090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an argument about the name, not the function, and irrelevant to what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>The name is very important, because evoking thoughts and feelings and responses from the players is important.<br /> <br /> A year ago, I was toying around with alternate methods of acquiring Heart's Blood and I asked the writers if it shouldn't just be called the victim's Essence instead. Robert Vance answered back that the name &quot;Heart's Blood&quot; was too powerful and important to the concept to drop.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777030#post777030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe still the method of drinking other Lunar's blood to learn forms***, though there's some issues with that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>would </i>like some method of gaining the stolen shapes another Lunar holds, but I also feel there's something too easy about them being able to freely share them.<br /> <br /> They can already freely <i>loan them out</i>, with Charms like Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique, where you get the form until the effect wears off or until you shift into another form.<br /> <br /> Lunars might even be able to learn a counter-Lunar Charm that substitutes any of their stolen forms for their own Heart's Blood, should a Lunar succeed in some form of non-lethal Hunt against them. &quot;You slept with me to take my face? Too bad! Here's that chicken I ate whole last week.&quot;<br /> <br /> That last trick doesn't even need to always be used as a trick. One Lunar wants the form of the prince the other Lunar ate last week, so they use the &quot;Swear an Oath&quot; Charm; the first Lunar fulfills some major or defining task for the other Lunar and magically receives the Heart's Blood when it is done. (There would need to be a clause preventing the second Lunar from -- or punishing the second Lunar for -- deliberately breaking such an oath to give the first Lunar the form without having to complete the task.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> **I do like Lunars as humans who are also bestial monsters. But as one caveat to this, I would be willing to say that this knack only works if it's consensual sexual intercourse. I'm sure the writers can think of a metaphysical reason for this (the target must on some level give of themselves, even if they don't realise they're giving their identity). I mean, I never knew anyone who was eaten by a cannibal, I have known people who've been victims of sexual assault, as I'm sure have most other players. </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I've never really considered the issue of Courtesan's Possession and rape because I've never considered myself or anyone using it for anything BUT consensual sex. Probably in no small part because of the very NAME -- you think of someone voluntarily coming to a courtesan for sex, or of a courtesan enticing someone to have sex with them, but not so much about a courtesan ambushing someone in a dark alley at night.<br /> <br /> So I have absolutely no problem with a new clause specifying that the Courtesan's Possession Hunt requires consensual sex as a more complete test of a Lunar's sexual hunting prowess than would be displayed with &quot;like the basic Hunt, but with rape instead of murder&quot;.<br /> <br /> The rape would be less of a &quot;proof&quot; than murder; killing the victim and tasting their blood is more complete, and a more thorough commitment to using violence and theft to get what you want. Compared to that, rape is half-hearted.<br /> <br /> Needing to persuade the target to have sex voluntarily is an entire different sort of Hunt, especially if there's a condition that your partner needs to find the experience satisfying. Then it becomes just as thorough a proof of commitment and prowess as hunting and killing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T08:32:31-08:00","id":777162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eurhetemec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777090#post777090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obvs. if the different Castes had different abilities they'd be called different things...</div> </div> </div> </div>Robert Vance, one of the writers for the game, is pretty sure the name will never change, precisely because of the function it is supposed to serve. A function which isn't just about what powers it grants to the Lunars, but also about the methods to which they need to resort in order to get those powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would argue that they want to have the capability to gain shapeshift forms, which is distinct from the &quot;hunt for Heart's Blood&quot; deal specifically. </div> </div> </div>I'm sure Sidereal players don't always want to have to carry around and use fragile paper slips for their Sutra Charms and bonuses, but it's pretty important to Sidereal themes and aesthetics that they need to rely on those anyway.<br /> <br /> Splat restraints close off options. That's the nature of having themes; NOT having other themes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a problem when killing things is the easiest, fastest and most direct way to get shapeshift forms. </div> </div> </div>But there are so many ways to kill things that don't involve doing it with your own two hands, and you're ignoring them.<br /> <br /> Consider the poster above who played a No Moon and said he was perfectly capable of using traps, poison, sorcery, or his own beast shapes to hunt and kill. His example should reassure those players who want to play No Moons but don't believe it would be that easy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, this isn't how Lunars are normally played. </div> </div> </div>It's not normal for Changing Moons to talk people into doing things for them, or to gather followers to do stuff for them? Or for No Moon sorcerors to throw fireballs?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;all-Lunar&quot; group is a rarely-seen thing. </div> </div> </div>But the &quot;single player in a player group&quot; is even more rarely seen.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if the Changing Moon is assisted by a Full Moon, a Dawn Caste Solar, a Dusk Caste Abyssal, or a Sworn Brotherhood of Terrestrials!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're also continuing to fail to understand that one Caste being way better than all the rest at something they all have to do is a problem. </div> </div> </div>You're continuing to fail to understand that &quot;killing&quot; can be accomplished in more ways than doing it with your own two hands.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You accepted that burden when you demanded a return to the 1E way of doing things </div> </div> </div>No, because you confuse <i>which </i>return I suggested.<br /> <br /> I suggested returning the emphasis of the requirements of the Hunt in Second Edition back to First Edition. A return which, contrary to your accusations against me, would actually make things easier on Changing Moons and No Moons than on Full Moons, because social and scholarly Lunars have so much more to gain than Full Moons, if they can rely on others or on tools to get the job done.<br /> <br /> Everything other change I suggested is a radical departure from both of the previous Editions and these suggestions are backed by what I feel are strong arguments and reasons.<br /> <br /> The rest of my essay isn't about pushing for change, but refuting the necessity of the changes that others have proposed, and those refutations are also, I feel, backed by strong arguments and reasons. Or at least strong enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure it's productive to suggest alternate methods for the other Castes unless your mind is open on this subject. </div> </div> </div>Likewise, it's not productive to argue against the validity of the basic Hunt unless your mind is open to considering how easily Changing Moons and No Moons can kill things in their own ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your current posts suggest it's closed, and that you have made up your mind that heart-eating is mandatory for everyone as the default. </div> </div> </div>Your posts have failed to put forward any counter proposals of your own, regarding what other methods Lunars might use which fulfill their themes as strongly as Heart's Blood Hunting.<br /> <br /> If you're just going to say I'm wrong and that you don't want what I want, then you're not actually contributing what you think you are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thief is a different archetype to Hunter as well </div> </div> </div>On what grounds? You can spare at least a sentence to explain how they are fundamentally different, just as I spent a sentence to explain how they were fundamentally the same. You also have to disprove my statement about their fundamental similarity, or how that similarity has no bearing on the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and in fact, mythically, the Thief and the Hunter are often at odds. </div> </div> </div>Again, back this up.<br /> <br /> But I will note that narratively, two hunters are as often at odds with each other as two thieves, when each wants what the other wants and neither wants to give it up.<br /> <br /> A thief and a hunter wouldn't be more at odds with each other than a thief and a farmer. The thief wants to take what the other man acquired with his own efforts, and the thief has to put forward his efforts to steal from them.<br /> <br /> The hunter is just as much of a thief if he is hunting the fox that the thief keeps as a pet, because the hunter has to kill the fox despite the thief's attempts to keep it safe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus Trickster is the RIGHT archetype for them. </div> </div> </div>Okay, red flag, stop the train.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunars are hunters&quot; is, like, <i>Assumption Zero</i> for this thread.<br /> <br /> If you were not prepared to accept that assumption, then you and I need to have an entirely different thread to debate whether not &quot;hunting&quot; is more central to the Lunar Exalted than &quot;deception&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T08:33:45-08:00","id":777163,"title":"","content":"Technically the Lunar only needs to be the one who kills the animal/person - if five hunters bring the caged bear on its last health level to the Lunar, and the Lunar stabs it and licks the blood off the knife, Heart's Blood acquired.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Blast, a Lunar ninja!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-30-2015, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T09:26:07-08:00","id":777190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robert Vance, one of the writers for the game, is pretty sure the name will never change, precisely because of the function it is supposed to serve. A function which isn't just about what powers it grants to the Lunars, but also about the methods to which they need to resort in order to get those powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't address my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure Sidereal players don't always want to have to carry around and use fragile paper slips for their Sutra Charms and bonuses, but it's pretty important to Sidereal themes and aesthetics that they need to rely on those anyway.<br /> <br /> Splat restraints close off options. That's the nature of having themes; NOT having other themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but it doesn't contradict what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are so many ways to kill things that don't involve doing it with your own two hands, and you're ignoring them.<br /> <br /> Consider the poster above who played a No Moon and said he was perfectly capable of using traps, poison, sorcery, or his own beast shapes to hunt and kill. His example should reassure those players who want to play No Moons but don't believe it would be that easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of which are less effective and reliable and, frankly, less easy than a typical Full Moon using their &quot;own hands&quot;. I've got a hardcore-social Solar - if I want someone or something non-trivial dead, in such a way that I am at the scene to take it's &quot;heart blood&quot;, no matter how well I play it or plan it, it's many times harder and more complex and less reliable than chucking the Dawn at it. Pretending otherwise is bloody silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not normal for Changing Moons to talk people into doing things for them, or to gather followers to do stuff for them? Or for No Moon sorcerors to throw fireballs?</div> </div> </div> </div>See above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter if the Changing Moon is assisted by a Full Moon, a Dawn Caste Solar, a Dusk Caste Abyssal, or a Sworn Brotherhood of Terrestrials!</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed and TBH the issue is more of a failure of theme than capability/possibility. IRL I don't expect No-Moons/Changing-Moons to be unable to every get HB with 1E-style rules. But I expect it to almost always look a bit weird compared to Full-Moons. Which it shouldn't have to. You shouldn't need to burn Charms just to be able to do things &quot;right&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're continuing to fail to understand that &quot;killing&quot; can be accomplished in more ways than doing it with your own two hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, and I'm honestly disappointed to see this kind of &quot;lolz&quot;-type response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggested returning the emphasis of the requirements of the Hunt in Second Edition back to First Edition. A return which, contrary to your accusations against me, would actually make things easier on Changing Moons and No Moons than on Full Moons, because social and scholarly Lunars have so much more to gain than Full Moons, if they can rely on others or on tools to get the job done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accusations? That seems a bit dramatic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, it's not productive to argue against the validity of the basic Hunt unless your mind is open to considering how easily Changing Moons and No Moons can kill things in their own ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have done and accept that it's viable, but that's not my big problem (less viable, for sure, though).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your posts have failed to put forward any counter proposals of your own, regarding what other methods Lunars might use which fulfill their themes as strongly as Heart's Blood Hunting.<br /> <br /> If you're just going to say I'm wrong and that you don't want what I want, then you're not actually contributing what you think you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, I'm not going to bother if you're just going to pick it apart, rather than be constructive. Which are you going to do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On what grounds? You can spare at least a sentence to explain how they are fundamentally different, just as I spent a sentence to explain how they were fundamentally the same. You also have to disprove my statement about their fundamental similarity, or how that similarity has no bearing on the Lunar Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't &quot;have to&quot; do anything here. But I will! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, back this up.</div> </div> </div> </div>No mythological Thief is also a Hunter. Trickster and Thief, are, however, synonymous:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_fictional_tricksters\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/Reynard-the-fox.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_fictional_tricksters\" target=\"_blank\"> List of fictional tricksters - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_fictional_tricksters\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_fictional_tricksters </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The trickster is the TARGET of the hunter, as with Bugs Bunny (and Road Runner and so on), if you want to go full-thrust pop-culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777162#post777162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, red flag, stop the train.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lunars are hunters&quot; is, like, <i>Assumption Zero</i> for this thread.<br /> <br /> If you were not prepared to accept that assumption, then you and I need to have an entirely different thread to debate whether not &quot;hunting&quot; is more central to the Lunar Exalted than &quot;deception&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing I didn't say that, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As I said, Trickster is the right archetype for <b><i>Changing-Moons, not all Lunars</i></b>. Is that even in debate? It's in their list of titles! Might not want to stop the train for things that aren't there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","name":"Eurhetemec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T04:02:36-08:00","id":777669,"title":"","content":"I would just love to be able to take the form of a child (for spying and stuff) and not have to have sex or murder involved.<br /> <br /> I played a Changing Moon for years. She hunted animals on occasion but never had a human alternate form until she learned the Courtesan's ways. And then she only took the forms of the people she legitimately cared for. It'd be really neat not to be so very restricted. Casual murder is really not a thing I tend to do with any character.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the absolute best way to get the form of pretty much any beast in second edition was to shoot it with an arrow and wait for it to bleed to death... since you know... they can't bandage themselves and any lethal damage would lead to bleeding and death. Note: I never actually did this, but I do think it's funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T04:40:56-08:00","id":777675,"title":"","content":"I don't have much personal investment in how Ex3 Lunars turn out, other than my prayers that they will somehow satisfy the eternal sobbing of their fans.<br /> <br /> Since you took the time to point it out, but kinda talk around it, though, I did want to make one observation a bit more directly. There are people who consider themselves Lunar fans,, who really are not Lunar fans. they want Mystique, or they want Cute/Sexy Cat Girl/Boy/Both, or whatever. But, Lunars are of Luna, the master Huntress, the ever-changing, etc etc. Her nature is bound up in blood, killing, and several other uncomfortable things that shiny friendly Solars gloss over. That's their intended role in the game.<br /> <br /> Far be it from me to tell people they are playing the game wrong, of course. I'm just making an observation as a somewhat disinterested observer, which is that some people want Lunars to be something they are not, and will not be. I think you nailed it on the head when you pointed out that Exigents fill that niche appropriately for people. Hopefully that splat will vent that desire for a tailored game experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T05:16:43-08:00","id":777684,"title":"","content":"I will note that my Changing Moon (originally Casteless) and largely pacifist Lunar courtesan got a ton of mileage out of his sex form-stealing knack, though I do think that I wouldn't have taken the &quot;beat someone up and steal their form one&quot; if I was the player then that I am now.<br /> <br /> To me, there's something important to be said about how viscerally the form-stealing rituals are - you drink of an animal's blood as it dies, allowing it to live on inside of you, or have sex, exchanging fluids and intense emotions and sensations with someone whose form you shall take. I think that I've read the devs saying that physicality is the default for Lunars, and killing and sex are two extremely <i>visceral</i> functions of the physical body. That said, I think that it will be much more viable in 3e to play a Lunar who shapeshifts only rarely (to flee the Wyld Hunt, for instance) while devoting most of his or her charms to doing whatever else they want to do. Lunars also tend to be broader than Solars in their focus - a Changing Moon trickster/manipulator will likely have at least a few excellencies in Mental and Physical Attributes, if nothing else, and Attributes are (as one might expect) rather broader than abilities.<br /> <br /> Having gone through all of that, I do think that I would love to have support for doing things that aren't purely physical with the Lunars - but I think that that will be fulfilled as well, likely with Mental charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T05:27:30-08:00","id":777686,"title":"","content":"I am honestly kind of nervous for the 3e Lunars.<br /> From what I've gathered, they are the leaders/gods/protectors of various barbarian tribes, they are trickster-shapeshifters-seducers who can infiltrate the Realm at will, they can be giant, terrifying beastmen who can fight armies single-handidly.<br /> They can take other creature's shapes by killing them and drinkin their blood, and can gain more ways to gain their shape.<br /> They can both become giant monsters through DBT and the tree connected to that (I assume it's more than one Charm), and a swordsman who uses his animalistic power to fuel his skill with his weapon.<br /> I assume every animal-form will have certain abilities that encourage the player to play that form, after all, why would I want to become a bear, if I have no benefit to becoming a bear?<br /> In addition to all this, there's whatever they are going to do with Chimera's.<br /> We know they are not going to be Were-Shoggoths who are in a constant state of flux.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel that, out of all the types of Exalted, the Lunars have gotten the biggest overhaul, and maybe that's what's making me uncertain.<br /> I guess the best way to solve that, for me, is to get some information on the signature Lunars of 3e. To sort of get an image of what they are, because right now, I really don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T05:31:06-08:00","id":777688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eurhetemec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777190#post777190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing I didn't say that, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As I said, Trickster is the right archetype for <b><i>Changing-Moons, not all Lunars</i></b>. Is that even in debate? It's in their list of titles! Might not want to stop the train for things that aren't there!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually, the Tricksters are the No Moons. The Changing Moon archetype is the Shaman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T05:34:51-08:00","id":777692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777686#post777686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I feel that, out of all the types of Exalted, the Lunars have gotten the biggest overhaul, and maybe that's what's making me uncertain.<br /> <br /> I guess the best way to solve that, for me, is to get some information on the signature Lunars of 3e. To sort of get an image of what they are, because right now, I really don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure the devs are still pinning down, really. I mean, the big pieces have to be in place, but the lower-level details/specifics, and the overall &quot;big picture&quot; is yet to be revealed, and indeed I don't expect us to have a really solid idea about what a Ex3 Lunar is like until the last few months before the Lunar book comes out.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that, whatever decisions they end up making, they'll end up with something great, and the best iteration of the Lunars yet (based on what they've said and how they've handled the Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777688#post777688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually, the Tricksters are the No Moons. The Changing Moon archetype is the Shaman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, mis-spoke, that's quite right!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","user":"Eurhetemec","date":". 12-01-2015, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","name":"Eurhetemec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T09:48:26-08:00","id":777798,"title":"","content":"Were I writing the Lunars from the ground up, I would probably have each of the three Castes approach the Hunt - and their default benefits from shapeshifting - differently.<br /> <br /> First, I'd have three means of &quot;hunting,&quot; each represented by a Charm (or, if we're keeping them, a Knack; for purposes of this discussion, I will use Charm, however, because I suspect we're not keeping the distinction). Each Caste would get a specific Hunting Charm for free, reflecting their method and the benefits they get from it.<br /> <br /> Tasting the Heart's Blood would be the Full Moon Charm, and would do more or less exactly what we're used to: grant physical shape, powers (e.g. wings-&gt;flight and claws-&gt;weapons) and Attributes. This version may require skinning the creature to wear its pelt as the form of shapeshifting, or maybe not. I'd have to think about it and look at the pros and cons.<br /> <br /> Name-Stealing Practice, the Charm of the Changing Moons, would involve getting to know the target, gaining their trust, and stepping in to fill their social shoes. It would gain their social Attributes and steal their very identity, while donning the appearance without, necessarily, changing species. A little awkward that Tepet Marcelus is keeping a young dog-boy as his pet, perhaps, but nobody questions it more than they did when it was his actual loyal hound, because all their Intimacies and experiences towards it are the same. The victim is still slain, left to die an empty husk wherever things utterly forgotten go.<br /> <br /> No Moons would have the Trickster's Bargain. Through artifice, trickery, and con artistry, the No Moon would trade and trick the target into yielding up his knowledge and wisdom, trading it away for metaphysical barter until he had nothing left in his head but pointless grey meat. This would permit the character to take on the mental guise of the victim, learning his knowledge, gaining his mental Attributes, and perhaps even stealing from his soul the mystical properties and authorities he once had (allowing him to learn Charms they might have had as Evocations, to some degree). Their mannerisms would remind people of the being they're emulating, though their form may not change at all. It is the mind and soul, not the body or the social ties, they have stolen.<br /> <br /> <br /> In all cases, learning another Caste's Charm enables you to assume those aspects of the creatures in your Library, as well, so a Lunar who knows all three would be able to perfectly step into the life, knowledge, and body of any creature in their Library. Knowing more than one also lets you choose the best way for you to perform your hunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:03:11-08:00","id":777875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777798#post777798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were I writing the Lunars from the ground up, I would probably have each of the three Castes approach the Hunt - and their default benefits from shapeshifting - differently.<br /> <br /> First, I'd have three means of &quot;hunting,&quot; each represented by a Charm (or, if we're keeping them, a Knack; for purposes of this discussion, I will use Charm, however, because I suspect we're not keeping the distinction). Each Caste would get a specific Hunting Charm for free, reflecting their method and the benefits they get from it.<br /> <br /> Tasting the Heart's Blood would be the Full Moon Charm, and would do more or less exactly what we're used to: grant physical shape, powers (e.g. wings-&gt;flight and claws-&gt;weapons) and Attributes. This version may require skinning the creature to wear its pelt as the form of shapeshifting, or maybe not. I'd have to think about it and look at the pros and cons.<br /> <br /> Name-Stealing Practice, the Charm of the Changing Moons, would involve getting to know the target, gaining their trust, and stepping in to fill their social shoes. It would gain their social Attributes and steal their very identity, while donning the appearance without, necessarily, changing species. A little awkward that Tepet Marcelus is keeping a young dog-boy as his pet, perhaps, but nobody questions it more than they did when it was his actual loyal hound, because all their Intimacies and experiences towards it are the same. The victim is still slain, left to die an empty husk wherever things utterly forgotten go.<br /> <br /> No Moons would have the Trickster's Bargain. Through artifice, trickery, and con artistry, the No Moon would trade and trick the target into yielding up his knowledge and wisdom, trading it away for metaphysical barter until he had nothing left in his head but pointless grey meat. This would permit the character to take on the mental guise of the victim, learning his knowledge, gaining his mental Attributes, and perhaps even stealing from his soul the mystical properties and authorities he once had (allowing him to learn Charms they might have had as Evocations, to some degree). Their mannerisms would remind people of the being they're emulating, though their form may not change at all. It is the mind and soul, not the body or the social ties, they have stolen.<br /> <br /> <br /> In all cases, learning another Caste's Charm enables you to assume those aspects of the creatures in your Library, as well, so a Lunar who knows all three would be able to perfectly step into the life, knowledge, and body of any creature in their Library. Knowing more than one also lets you choose the best way for you to perform your hunts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those... those are really interesting ways. Personally I would prefer that the player choose one of them regardless of caste, as I can see characters from each caste (A bit harder with the Full Moon, but still) that would choose a different one then their default out of those three. Not often, and wouldn't be the normal way, but I could see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:11:47-08:00","id":777879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bulshock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777875#post777875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Those... those are really interesting ways. Personally I would prefer that the player choose one of them regardless of caste, as I can see characters from each caste (A bit harder with the Full Moon, but still) that would choose a different one then their default out of those three. Not often, and wouldn't be the normal way, but I could see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. They're rough ideas. I would answer, were I designing it, the players who wanted one of the other methods but to be of a different caste, that they should just spend a Charm on getting the method they want. Nothing says they have to use the one they got for free preferentially, and nothing says they had to &quot;learn&quot; the second one by any means other than having it at Exaltation, since Exalts often have a few Charms right at that moment. It's all about how they use their Essence, especially if they're going to emphasize in this edition that Charms are NOT in-game constructs. For him, he just instinctively grasped two ways to do it, and preferred one over the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:57:22-08:00","id":777925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777688#post777688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, actually, the Tricksters are the No Moons. The Changing Moon archetype is the Shaman.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have that backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:07:36-08:00","id":777930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777925#post777925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have that backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2015/09/27/lunar-exalted-what-are-they-to-you-thread-summary/\" target=\"_blank\">Don't be so sure.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Lunar Exalted: What Are They To You?&quot; Thread Summary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Grande\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>LordofArcana</i>:<br /> I was thinking about the Lunar castes, and it seems like while Full-Moons are great, that the No-Moons and Changing-Moons are reversed.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Grande\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Shamans, as I understand them, rely almost entirely upon having a personal relationship with the spirits/monsters/things that they interact with. They need to be able to make just about anyone feel comfortable with them, because they will frequently deal with powerful things that can have rather short tempers or odd perspectives. That suggests really impressive interpersonal skills and thus Changing-Moons.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Grande\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tricksters, on the other hand, are generally widely disliked. They generally influence people and situations by finding an opportunity to be a manipulative bastard and taking full advantage of it. They are almost always clever and perceptive, and often quite intelligent. To me that suggests No-Moon.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Grande\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>John</i>:<br /> Very thoughtful observation.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:54:05-08:00","id":777953,"title":"","content":"A thread for Trickster/Shaman Caste discussions exists here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/414129-the-no-moon-is-the-trickster-and-the-changing-moon-is-the-shaman\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-is-the-shaman</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T21:44:50-08:00","id":778105,"title":"","content":"A developer thinks that an argument is interesting. That does not equal it being a fact.<br /> <br /> To my knowledge, it's never been said that Changing Moon and No Moon are actually switching roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T21:57:17-08:00","id":778111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778105#post778105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A developer thinks that an argument is interesting. That does not equal it being a fact.<br /> <br /> To my knowledge, it's never been said that Changing Moon and No Moon are actually switching roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is strenuously arguing that they should.<br /> <br /> The No Moon's sorcery and the fact that anti-spirit Charms are likely staying in Perception, and the Changing Moon's ability to lie to people with Manipulation, means that they would always retain some trickery and shamanism.<br /> <br /> But seeing Changing Moons as shamans too and No Moons as tricksters too helps fill out their Caste-favored Charm sets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T22:01:29-08:00","id":778112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777798#post777798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Name-Stealing Practice, the Charm of the Changing Moons, would involve getting to know the target, gaining their trust, and stepping in to fill their social shoes. It would gain their social Attributes and steal their very identity, while donning the appearance without, necessarily, changing species. A little awkward that Tepet Marcelus is keeping a young dog-boy as his pet, perhaps, but nobody questions it more than they did when it was his actual loyal hound, because all their Intimacies and experiences towards it are the same. The victim is still slain, left to die an empty husk wherever things utterly forgotten go.<br /> <br /> No Moons would have the Trickster's Bargain. Through artifice, trickery, and con artistry, the No Moon would trade and trick the target into yielding up his knowledge and wisdom, trading it away for metaphysical barter until he had nothing left in his head but pointless grey meat. This would permit the character to take on the mental guise of the victim, learning his knowledge, gaining his mental Attributes, and perhaps even stealing from his soul the mystical properties and authorities he once had (allowing him to learn Charms they might have had as Evocations, to some degree). Their mannerisms would remind people of the being they're emulating, though their form may not change at all. It is the mind and soul, not the body or the social ties, they have stolen.</div> </div> </div> </div>...But where is the shapeshifting? Where do the animal totems and general animal association come in? Why are you playing as these characters instead of Solars with Supernal Socialize and the personae Charms?<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are supposed to be very physical and beastly. Every Lunar is reborn with the power to physically transform into an animal, regardless of what Caste they will eventually have.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me (even I forget) that there cannot be a Caste-dependent method of Heart's Blood Hunting when Lunar Exalted take their Second Breath without having any Caste at all. All Lunars would need a universal method during this transitional period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T22:01:48-08:00","id":778113,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing against a hypothetical mingling of their roles, I'm arguing against <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, actually, the Tricksters are the No Moons. The Changing Moon archetype is the Shaman. </div> </div> </div>No one who creates the game (again, to my knowledge) ever said that. So one should not go around telling people that this is the case. Only that it <i>may be</i> the case in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T05:30:09-08:00","id":778260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778113#post778113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not arguing against a hypothetical mingling of their roles, I'm arguing against<br /> <br /> No one who creates the game (again, to my knowledge) ever said that. So one should not go around telling people that this is the case. Only that it <i>may be</i> the case in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel less bad about being confused on this now, for sure! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","name":"Eurhetemec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T05:35:24-08:00","id":778261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778112#post778112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which reminds me (even I forget) that there cannot be a Caste-dependent method of Heart's Blood Hunting when Lunar Exalted take their Second Breath without having any Caste at all. All Lunars would need a universal method during this transitional period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that's canon in Ex3, that's a very good point, actually, and changes my perspective a bit.<br /> <br /> In that case, we could have all Lunars have Heart's Blood (as you suggested), and then all Lunars gain a further non-Charm method when they get their Caste. That seems like a win/win to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8973-eurhetemec","name":"Eurhetemec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T06:35:04-08:00","id":778292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778112#post778112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...But where is the shapeshifting? Where do the animal totems and general animal association come in? Why are you playing as these characters instead of Solars with Supernal Socialize and the personae Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I was unclear. The Full Moon one involves full-on shape-assumption. The Changing Moon one, as I'm envisioning it, involves taking on superficial characteristics necessary to fill certain details, but is mostly a change of the shape of one's Fate and social presence. The No Moon one also involves shapechange, but of the mind and soul. You WILL resemble the creature you take on the mental and spiritual form of, but more due to having that indefinable personna of them. I admit, this diminishes the inherent physical shapeshifting a bit by defocusing it, though getting it is as easy as picking the right caste or grabbing the right charm at chargen. It also lets those who keep complaining that they don't WANT to have to be animals elude it.<br /> <br /> That said, you're right: the spirit totem is not addressed here. I will need to think more on it. As I said, this was a very rough draft of something I've idly pondered but never e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778112#post778112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which reminds me (even I forget) that there cannot be a Caste-dependent method of Heart's Blood Hunting when Lunar Exalted take their Second Breath without having any Caste at all. All Lunars would need a universal method during this transitional period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a valid point, assuming unfixed castes remain a thing in 3e. I think, though, as a first try at it, if you do'nt have a fixed Caste, you gain the hunting Charm of the Caste you're in at any given moment. Casteless shift Castes with the phases of the moon, after all. So during the full moon, you have the Hearts Blood hunt; during the new moon, you have the mind-and-soul trickster's bargain; during the changing phases, you steal their name and fate. And, likewise, the nature of your shapeshifting changes to match. Obviously, buying one or more of the Charms would let you use that one's hunt and shifting all the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:25:45-08:00","id":778388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eurhetemec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778261#post778261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that's canon in Ex3, that's a very good point, actually, and changes my perspective a bit.<br /> <br /> In that case, we could have all Lunars have Heart's Blood (as you suggested), and then all Lunars gain a further non-Charm method when they get their Caste. That seems like a win/win to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have <i>much</i> fewer problems with this.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem is &quot;what do you consider appropriate Heart's Blood Hunting methods for each Caste?&quot;<br /> <br /> (I'm not talking about Segev's &quot;emulate the victim socially or mentally&quot; idea, I'm talking about taking the HEART'S BLOOD, complete with the entire physical form, with any social or mental traits being accessed through social and mental Charms.)<br /> <br /> Not every Changing Moon is going to (or <i>should </i>have to) sleep around for forms. Other Changing Moons could form bonds with familiars and mortals, gaining their Heart's Blood as they recognize him as their lord and master; the beastmaster Lunar might even be able to gain Heart's Blood from creatures that his <i>familiars</i> kill. Still other Changing Moons could gain forms through deals and exchanges backed by magical oaths -- acquiring Heart's Blood by fulfilling a Major or Defining task as a service, or stealing the Heart's Blood if the second party breaks the agreement.<br /> <br /> Even the &quot;agree to a contest of skill or luck&quot; idea for gaining Heart's Blood seems like a Changing Moon Charm, based on how similar it is to the oath-related Charm. The Lunar is trying to convince someone to consent to a contest of skill or luck, with agreed-upon rules of play and conditions for victory.<br /> <br /> There's no single &quot;Changing Moon hunt&quot; that I can see; each of these applies to one archetypical character concept and not necessarily any of the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> What would be a non-lethal method of Heart's Blood Hunting rooted in the <i>Physical</i> Attributes? Killing is the default. Rape instead of killing is right out; it's simultaneously too &quot;easy&quot; and too skeevy. Beating someone unconscious instead of killing is weak-sauce and is more interesting as an application of the &quot;agree to a contest&quot; Hunt.<br /> <br /> At least for Mental Attributes, Robert Vance's &quot;I steal your face by suing you&quot; is Intelligence-based.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also the problem that not all of these Charms are entry-level. Vance's Charm requires you have the Charm for using human Heart's Blood. The oath Charms probably need to start with a Charm that creates an Intimacy to the terms of the oath in the Lunar before the Lunar can learn Charms to derive other benefits from the oaths. Gaining Heart's Blood from familiars and human vassals might follow after the oath Charm as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:35:18-08:00","id":778397,"title":"","content":"If the Changing Moon keeps their Anima power, their hunt could be a social stalking of the character, learning his interactions, and eventually taking the heart's blood of his social life by using their Anima to step into it, driving him out and reclaiming all of the Initmacies people have for him for the Lunar's use.<br /> <br /> This works less well with animal forms, though. Doable, to an extent, but less satisfying and getting weirder the more solitary the animal in question tends to be. Plus, imitating an ant to convince its colony you're a member is... silly-seeming. (Though I suppose, so is hunting the ideal ant to eat the &quot;heart's blood&quot; equivalent of.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T10:28:25-08:00","id":778440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778397#post778397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Changing Moon keeps their Anima power, their hunt could be a social stalking of the character, learning his interactions, and eventually taking the heart's blood of his social life by using their Anima to step into it, driving him out and reclaiming all of the Initmacies people have for him for the Lunar's use.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would also require the Prey's Skin Disguise Charm for hunting humans / using human Heart's Blood. So, no good as an anima power, even leaving aside my arguments about why it's a bad anima power.<br /> <br /> Plus, the end goal is blurry. &quot;Knock off someone's last Health Level&quot; is mechanically simple, and &quot;it's dead, you killed it&quot; is narratively simple.<br /> <br /> In your suggested method, HOW much does the Lunar have to replace his target before he finally gets the target's Heart's Blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T11:11:38-08:00","id":778470,"title":"","content":"I'd say he'd have to supplant every Intimacy towards the target held by anybody towards whom the target holds an Intimacy. I'd say &quot;reciprocated Intimacies,&quot; but that's not quite right, because &quot;My teacher (respect)&quot; would be enough to require you to get his teacher's Intimacies of &quot;My pupil (frustrated romantic interest)&quot; and &quot;My pupil (guilt for having failed to save his older brother from the Wyld Hunt)&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:08:06-08:00","id":778584,"title":"","content":"I don't see a problem with Lunars defaulting to killing stuff to get new forms. A Lunar who is good at killing stuff will get more forms, sure, but only from stuff she can already kill. A less capable combatant would struggle to get as many powerful combat forms, which strikes me as completely fair and reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:12:10-08:00","id":778587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=777675#post777675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you took the time to point it out, but kinda talk around it, though, I did want to make one observation a bit more directly. There are people who consider themselves Lunar fans,, who really are not Lunar fans. they want Mystique, or they want Cute/Sexy Cat Girl/Boy/Both, or whatever. But, Lunars are of Luna, the master Huntress, the ever-changing, etc etc. Her nature is bound up in blood, killing, and several other uncomfortable things that shiny friendly Solars gloss over. That's their intended role in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not very cool to respond to pages old posts, and I fully expect this to be regarded as totally unhelpful, but I did want to point out that what Luna is has probably changed a lot* over these books, and how the latest depiction is either current to 3e, or reflected in Lunars 3e is, I think, pretty arbitrary. <br /> <br /> (What's the implied Luna like in 1e or 2e Lunars? If you like the GotMH Luna better, how much of that is just due to John Morke writing it shiny, rather than stronger base concepts? How much does this even matter compared to Lunars being appealing and likeable as playable characters?)<br /> <br /> Roughly, I have as much sympathy with much of this line of arguments as &quot;Well... the Unconquered Sun *is* the god of War and holy wrath... What do you mean you want to play a pacifistic Solar, or a Solar with choice in whether you apply violence or not?&quot; Individual Exalted are many things their gods are; and many things they are not. (And the mainline Big 5 Exalted exist a lot more to enable genre archetypes than realize the mythos of any of the Incarna...)<br /> <br /> I'm definitely not someone who thinks of myself as a big Lunars fan though either, so this isn't a huge issue to me though... <br /> <br /> (Really with &quot;sacrifice&quot; and &quot;predation&quot; based magic powers, generally, as someone who isn't too interested in Lunars, if you did pursue that route a lot for Lunars, and I reckon you might potentially just get Terrifying Argent Witches, maybe with less interesting magic... I think for the devs and those just crafting ideas in their head it's probably worth looking at how central the ideas of Lunars are fundamentally predatory were to that fan interpretation of Lunars and how that guided the end result, and the tone it had...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:21:53-08:00","id":778632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778587#post778587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much does this even matter compared to Lunars being appealing and likeable as playable characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who's been a Lunars fan since 1e, I find that Lunars <i>are</i> likable as trangressive, visceral counterpoints to idealised-nigh-angelic Solars. A part of that transgressiveness includes heart-eating and cannibalism, and I think it goes a long way to showing the kinds of things a Lunar will do to succeed. There's a deep stomach churning fear, that Solars don't really create, in having to beg for your life to a shape-shifting monster that you know, deep within your trembling bones, <i>will eat you</i> (of course, this being Fantasy, the people getting eaten usually have it coming to them through being callous and cruel in a way only possible in a world where everything is turned to 11).<br /> <br /> I (personally, and this goes to reinforce the thread's thesis) see Lunars as, basically, anarchists. Not in a teenage-rebellion way, mind you, but in a real &quot;cooperation without leadership, compassion without societal obligation, decentralised resistence&quot;* way; which makes them fickle and dangerous from the point of view of those raised in more structured/stratified society.<br /> <br /> Or sometimes you just want to play a legendary monster and don't want to deal with the angst and Humanity of world of darkness.<br /> <br /> *I'm not writing an anarchist manifesto, just some thematics to get the idea across","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:52:01-08:00","id":778651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778584#post778584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a problem with Lunars defaulting to killing stuff to get new forms. A Lunar who is good at killing stuff will get more forms, sure, but only from stuff she can already kill. A less capable combatant would struggle to get as many powerful combat forms, which strikes me as completely fair and reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, y'know, take some investment into social Attributes, get some dots in Resources, and pay local hunters and trappers to bring you live specimens. Sure, a bear is generally a tough fight, but it's not likely to kill you when it's in a cage and you have a spear.<br /> <br /> (Though this method is unlikely to ever get you a Tyrant Lizard form. For that I suggest waiting until you find your Dawn Caste mate and convincing him to bring you one as a sign of his love for you.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:56:17-08:00","id":778654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778651#post778651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, y'know, take some investment into social Attributes, get some dots in Resources, and pay local hunters and trappers to bring you live specimens. Sure, a bear is generally a tough fight, but it's not likely to kill you when it's in a cage and you have a spear.<br /> <br /> (Though this method is unlikely to ever get you a Tyrant Lizard form. For that I suggest waiting until you find your Dawn Caste mate and convincing him to bring you one as a sign of his love for you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Darling, I simply MUST have a Tyrant Lizard to wear to the battle this spring. One of the feathered kind; I will NOT go out in that musty old Yeddim I've had for the last three seasons!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:59:31-08:00","id":778659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778651#post778651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, y'know, take some investment into social Attributes, get some dots in Resources, and pay local hunters and trappers to bring you live specimens. Sure, a bear is generally a tough fight, but it's not likely to kill you when it's in a cage and you have a spear.<br /> <br /> (Though this method is unlikely to ever get you a Tyrant Lizard form. For that I suggest waiting until you find your Dawn Caste mate and convincing him to bring you one as a sign of his love for you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah what's weird to me is people signing up to play Pretty Kitty and then getting annoyed at having to use Pretty Kitty methods to do stuff. Idk if it's just a forum thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:06:24-08:00","id":778664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778659#post778659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah what's weird to me is people signing up to play Pretty Kitty and then getting annoyed at having to use Pretty Kitty methods to do stuff. Idk if it's just a forum thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's weird to me is how<i> viciously </i>unreceptive some folks were to this idea last time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:22:41-08:00","id":778670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778632#post778632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who's been a Lunars fan since 1e, I find that Lunars <i>are</i> likable as trangressive, visceral counterpoints to idealised-nigh-angelic Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem though like you need idealised nigh-angelic Solars, who are kind of un-visceral and sanitised, for that. I'm not sure if that's what we've got! (Or if that's what we'd want even if we could get it). It seems like sort of a different ball game being the visceral counterpart to the floaty, idealised, ethereal, unrealistic shining heroes who won't stoop to deal with reality, than being the visceral counterpart to a splat that already contains quite visceral, bloodied and tough barbarian fantasy heroes and are modally along the lines of being rough, ready and worldly heroes (although I get that there's still a huge gap between that and a shapeshifting ohmygod boundary and category defying gloriously bastardised monster-man).<br /> \u200b<br /> I found your post pretty good at helping me understand that the appeal of the Lunars to probably many their fans is in those elements of monstrousness and links between transformation and transgression (and between transgression and true freedom). Unsure still about how much of that is or should be a) linked to the idea of all Lunar characters needing capabilities that key off sacrificing or consuming others for your own power and b) how general the appeal of transgression and predation is to all the Lunar fans (how many do and how many are interested in ideas more along the lines of protection and escape and transformation than transgression or monstrosity?). Glad I'm not in the position to have to feel out the audience and balance this with lots of wider concenrs, then make any decisive choices, unlike the actual writers.<br /> <br /> Re: Pretty Kitties, just as a notion, I wonder if some of that is the difference between lots of people enjoying the idea of playing a character who is casually socially powerful because of their beauty, yet at the same time disliking people who calculatedly use their own beauty? Kind of like unconscious charisma vs conscious manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:44:02-08:00","id":778684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778670#post778670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does seem though like you need idealised nigh-angelic Solars, who are kind of un-visceral and sanitised, for that. I'm not sure if that's what we've got! (Or if that's what we'd want even if we could get it). It seems like sort of a different ball game being the visceral counterpart to the floaty, idealised, ethereal, unrealistic shining heroes who won't stoop to deal with reality, than being the visceral counterpart to a splat that already contains quite visceral, bloodied and tough barbarian fantasy heroes and are modally along the lines of being rough, ready and worldly heroes (although I get that there's still a huge gap between that and a shapeshifting ohmygod boundary and category defying gloriously bastardised monster-man).<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted my point of view is potentially mired in 2e-isms; however, Solars still have &quot;heroic&quot; baggage (from an inter-player perspective), where you're still expected to act like a decent-ish human being. In my experience with Lunars, you have much more freedom in your approach because &quot;meh, Lunars gonna Lune.&quot; A player playing a Solar cannibal is frowned upon (from my limited obsevations) and makes players uncomfortable, but similar Lunars are much more readily accepted and the roleplaying that comes with it is more readily participated in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778670#post778670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Pretty Kitties, just as a notion, I wonder if some of that is the difference between lots of people enjoying the idea of playing a character who is casually socially powerful because of their beauty, yet at the same time disliking people who calculatedly use their own beauty? Kind of like unconscious charisma vs conscious manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to say the same: I think it hits on a cognitive dissonance endemic to modern culture (though probably not globally), where conventionally attractive people are supposed to act like they don't know they're attractive, because using their beauty to their advantage is considered manipulative and exploitative. But as the player, you <i>can't</i> &quot;not know&quot;, because you chose the stats, and they're right there on the sheet, so you always know that you're using your beauty to your advantage. For many people, that's fine; but for some it creates cognitive dissonance, because they're trying to play a &quot;good&quot; person while acting out behaviours that society demonises.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778654#post778654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Darling, I simply MUST have a Tyrant Lizard to wear to the battle this spring. One of the feathered kind; I will NOT go out in that musty old Yeddim I've had for the last three seasons!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>................. why did I read that in Rarity's voice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-02-2015, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:52:49-08:00","id":778691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778684#post778684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For many people, that's fine; but for some it creates cognitive dissonance, because they're trying to play a &quot;good&quot; person while acting out behaviours that society demonises.</div> </div> </div> </div>While perhaps true, this seems especially jarring for a game about playing classical-type heroes in a savage age - I have yet to play a character in Exalted that doesn't engage in behaviors that society demonizes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T16:56:15-08:00","id":778696,"title":"","content":"The devs seem pretty set on Lunars as monsters this time around, and I think that will drive the stories you can tell with them. Earlier someone brought up the inconvenience of taking on a child's form without doing something monstrous. That looks deliberate to me. Maybe your character will take on a child's form by finding someone who is sick beyond saving and convincing herself that death is merciful. She's gonna have a time with the actual tasting of the Heart's Blood, assuming no charms, but hey, that's what a monster would do. That doesn't mean every Lunar is a wanton child murderer by design. It just means they will sometimes have a reason to do something monstrous, and perhaps think about how to mitigate it or make up for it. Or in other cases how to rationalize, pretend nothing happened, and move on. Or in yet other cases to slide into more horrifying habits. Seems like the point of all this is to examine those themes, not ditch them when they get in the way of overcoming challenges as the player sees fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T17:01:21-08:00","id":778699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778691#post778691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While perhaps true, this seems especially jarring for a game about playing classical-type heroes in a savage age - I have yet to play a character in Exalted that doesn't engage in behaviors that society demonizes.</div> </div> </div> </div>For that matter, I myself <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polyamory\" target=\"_blank\">engage</a> in behaviors that society demonizes, and I don't think I'm alone on this forum, either. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-03-2015, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T18:39:15-08:00","id":778735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778691#post778691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While perhaps true, this seems especially jarring for a game about playing classical-type heroes in a savage age - I have yet to play a character in Exalted that doesn't engage in behaviors that society demonizes.</div> </div> </div> </div>To avoid beating around the bush, I'm talking about things like internalized misogyny, which I've actually seen metaphorically tear a player's character apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-02-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T18:41:40-08:00","id":778736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778696#post778696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs seem pretty set on Lunars as monsters this time around, and I think that will drive the stories you can tell with them. Earlier someone brought up the inconvenience of taking on a child's form without doing something monstrous. That looks deliberate to me. Maybe your character will take on a child's form by finding someone who is sick beyond saving and convincing herself that death is merciful. She's gonna have a time with the actual tasting of the Heart's Blood, assuming no charms, but hey, that's what a monster would do. That doesn't mean every Lunar is a wanton child murderer by design. It just means they will sometimes have a reason to do something monstrous, and perhaps think about how to mitigate it or make up for it. Or in other cases how to rationalize, pretend nothing happened, and move on. Or in yet other cases to slide into more horrifying habits. Seems like the point of all this is to examine those themes, not ditch them when they get in the way of overcoming challenges as the player sees fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The Lunar is an outsider to human culture, breaking taboos (cannibalism, bestiality). But, at the same time, the setting sets them up as &quot;heroes&quot; against the Realm's &quot;villains&quot; which I find is interesting.<br /> And certainly, looking at the Lunar PCs in the games I run/play, they do engage with these themes with reluctance in quite an interesting way.<br /> It's why I dislike the knack for gaining forms by just knocking people out. You're playing a monster-hero, for goodness' sake!<br /> <br /> I would say that polyamory is not a great example though Alucard, because it's something that some societies do accept (perhaps in the more formal form of polygamy or polyandry), and which is semi-acceptable in our society (I mean, I know a whole bunch of people who do it, or have done it; which makes me wonder, what is the link between roleplayers and polyamory? There's got to be a sociology paper in that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T20:19:24-08:00","id":778780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778736#post778736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. The Lunar is an outsider to human culture, breaking taboos (cannibalism, bestiality). But, at the same time, the setting sets them up as &quot;heroes&quot; against the Realm's &quot;villains&quot; which I find is interesting.<br /> And certainly, looking at the Lunar PCs in the games I run/play, they do engage with these themes with reluctance in quite an interesting way.<br /> It's why I dislike the knack for gaining forms by just knocking people out. You're playing a monster-hero, for goodness' sake!</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of what has made Lunars tough to pin down is their reliance on someone else to define them. The Lunar used to be, say, the senator's even more devious and scheming spouse, or the mob boss's fixer who always finds a way (you don't want to know what it was), or the police lieutenant's skull-cracking sergeant. As impressive as those characters can be, they're also guided by someone else whose glory they live for, and who points them in a good direction. What happens when that person goes away though, when that brutal efficiency and sense of purpose has nowhere to go? What do those characters do in the spotlight? It's not pretty.<br /> <br /> As much as I rolled my eyes at 2e for constant, &quot;My my my, that's a biiiiig problem. Might take the united Exalted host to fix this!&quot; situations, I do still like that the absence of the Solars has broken things, and not just the N/A artifacts they made. Everyone is at each other's throats, and no one is right. That the Solars have to fix this (or else) is OK as long as that doesn't have to happen by next Tuesday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:04:42-08:00","id":778806,"title":"","content":"Lunars have a special problem; the community doesn't know what we want from them. Almost everything about them to date is considered divisive. The only thing we are united on is that the previous iterations have problems, though which elements are problematic and how...terminal they are have been the center of many debates.<br /> <br /> It is made harder because the many conceptions of Lunars have led to a plethora of compelling concepts, often mutually exclusive. The ideal Lunar splat would let you play; the Monster, the Outsider, the Barbarian, the Infiltrator, the Power behind the Throne, the Dionysian Witch-Queen, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolverine_(character)\" target=\"_blank\">Wolverine</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider-Man\" target=\"_blank\">Spiderman</a>, the (fake) tribal spirit, the Frontier Lord, the Warden of Worlds, the Inhuman Genius as well as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_Man\" target=\"_blank\">Animal Man</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beast_Boy\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling/Beast Boy</a>.<br /> <br /> Until we get (official) Lunars that are fantastic enough to unite the fandom, we are not going to be happy with any Lunars...we don't know how a 'good' Lunar works, let alone looks like.<br /> <br /> Additionally a lot of prior baggage means Lunars are perceived to be lesser actors, with less agency than most other Exalted. Which is almost universally decried as awful but certain relationships (such as the Solar Bond) have been portrayed as fundamental to the concept. Being defined by a relationship is a highly unhealthy in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:16:48-08:00","id":778810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778736#post778736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that polyamory is not a great example though Alucard\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>It's me, though. I don't eat people to gain their forms or breed people with animals to produce monstrous armies in real life, but I <i>am</i> polyamorous.<br /> <br /> And I still get a lot of shit flung at me for it, even if there are people and places that are cool with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:45:49-08:00","id":778817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778587#post778587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not very cool to respond to pages old posts, and I fully expect this to be regarded as totally unhelpful, but I did want to point out that what Luna is has probably changed a lot* over these books, and how the latest depiction is either current to 3e, or reflected in Lunars 3e is, I think, pretty arbitrary.<br /> <br /> (What's the implied Luna like in 1e or 2e Lunars? If you like the GotMH Luna better, how much of that is just due to John Morke writing it shiny, rather than stronger base concepts? How much does this even matter compared to Lunars being appealing and likeable as playable characters?)<br /> <br /> Roughly, I have as much sympathy with much of this line of arguments as &quot;Well... the Unconquered Sun *is* the god of War and holy wrath... What do you mean you want to play a pacifistic Solar, or a Solar with choice in whether you apply violence or not?&quot; Individual Exalted are many things their gods are; and many things they are not. (And the mainline Big 5 Exalted exist a lot more to enable genre archetypes than realize the mythos of any of the Incarna...)<br /> <br /> I'm definitely not someone who thinks of myself as a big Lunars fan though either, so this isn't a huge issue to me though...<br /> <br /> (Really with &quot;sacrifice&quot; and &quot;predation&quot; based magic powers, generally, as someone who isn't too interested in Lunars, if you did pursue that route a lot for Lunars, and I reckon you might potentially just get Terrifying Argent Witches, maybe with less interesting magic... I think for the devs and those just crafting ideas in their head it's probably worth looking at how central the ideas of Lunars are fundamentally predatory were to that fan interpretation of Lunars and how that guided the end result, and the tone it had...)</div> </div> </div> </div>You are of course correct that Luna's character is arbitrary, and could be changed to be anything in a new edition. Heck, it's valid to point out that Luna's personality at any given moment is arbitrary!<br /> <br /> I'm not particularly attached to one vision of Luna, either. But, near as I can recall, she has always been a primal, sensual, predatory figure. And I was essentially agreeing with the OP that in some cases the complaints about Lunars seem to point to the notion that people don't like what Lunars are. Again, I don't say this to rag on anyone's fun, or claim I know the right Exalted.<br /> <br /> To me, it's a bit like people saying Solars are too vanilla, or Dragon-Bloods aren't Avatar enough etc. At a certain point, it's helpful to acknowledge that each Exalt type is really enabling a certain kind of story, or stories. If someone doesn't really like that story, then maybe that splat overall isn't for them. It can be fun to play deliberately against type (Vegetarian Lunar, etc), and none of those themes or story experiences are straight jackets, but Solars are <i>intended</i> be Vanilla, and Lunars are <i>intended</i> to invoke themes of predation, monstrosity, etc. I don't think that's really going to change. If someone just wants an omni-shifter, they probably really want an Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T00:41:39-08:00","id":778842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778810#post778810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's me, though. I don't eat people to gain their forms or breed people with animals to produce monstrous armies in real life, but I <i>am</i> polyamorous.<br /> <br /> And I still get a lot of shit flung at me for it, even if there are people and places that are cool with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I misunderstood your original point, kind of. I thought you were using polyamory as an example of the sort of thing Lunars do that are considered taboo (my point was it probably isn't very taboo in many Exalted societies), but I guess you were saying that &quot;players feel cognitive dissonance because they are trying to play a good character while doing actions society demonises&quot; is a bad point, because what society demonises and what is actually bad are not the same thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-03-2015, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T00:47:49-08:00","id":778845,"title":"","content":"Actually, my polyamory was an aside. You'll notice I didn't bring it up when I made my point, which was that the notion that people are trying to play &quot;good people&quot; seems at odds with the premise of the game; to me, if you come in with the intent of playing a shining knight all dressed in white (which I generally don't), it's for the sake of seeing what happens when he gets mud splattered all over his cuirass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-03-2015, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T07:11:57-08:00","id":778986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778696#post778696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs seem pretty set on Lunars as monsters this time around, and I think that will drive the stories you can tell with them. Earlier someone brought up the inconvenience of taking on a child's form without doing something monstrous. That looks deliberate to me. Maybe your character will take on a child's form by finding someone who is sick beyond saving and convincing herself that death is merciful. She's gonna have a time with the actual tasting of the Heart's Blood, assuming no charms, but hey, that's what a monster would do. That doesn't mean every Lunar is a wanton child murderer by design. It just means they will sometimes have a reason to do something monstrous, and perhaps think about how to mitigate it or make up for it. Or in other cases how to rationalize, pretend nothing happened, and move on. Or in yet other cases to slide into more horrifying habits. Seems like the point of all this is to examine those themes, not ditch them when they get in the way of overcoming challenges as the player sees fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in the &quot;be a child&quot; case, unless they're impersonating a specific child (in which case they were going to murder somebody anyway, whether it's a child or not, if they're impersonating specific people), there might be a Lunar Charm this time around that allows them to alter the physical age of the form they're wearing. Probably Appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T07:17:54-08:00","id":778990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778845#post778845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, my polyamory was an aside. You'll notice I didn't bring it up when I made my point, which was that the notion that people are trying to play &quot;good people&quot; seems at odds with the premise of the game; to me, if you come in with the intent of playing a shining knight all dressed in white (which I generally don't), it's for the sake of seeing what happens when he gets mud splattered all over his cuirass.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, I misunderstood your point, sorry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T07:22:00-08:00","id":778992,"title":"","content":"I wrote an essay, once, on Lunars as the Other, which was on the old forums and on the wiki, but sadly, I don't think I had a personal copy of it that survived the computer-swaps from then until now.<br /> <br /> The idea, though, was that Lunars can be ally or enemy, rival or coconspirator, friend or nemesis, even to those whom they support or undermine. They can do the more traditional forms of allegiance and opposition, being an open and honest friend to bolster and aid, or a clear and present danger to rip apart those they oppose. But they have a tremendous capacity to aid those for whom they care by being the enemy who sharpens them, the rival who keeps them on their toes, or the terror that constrains them from self-destructive behavior. They also have a horrifying facility to destroy by being close, cloying, trusted aids who cut all support and undermine and encourage their hated ones to destroy themselves, with their despised victim thanking them for it all the way.<br /> <br /> My favorite example that I can remember is a Lunar-as-Monster who protects a village. Taboos about going out at night, about entering certain parts of the surrounding woods, and about how and when to greet visitors all spring up from the fact that there is a horrifying Monster that dwells in the dark. It lurks just on the edge of vision, and attacks those who transgress the taboos the village has pieced together. But it is also the ONLY threat to the village; nothing else that would threaten it dares draw near. Bandits break the taboos and are destroyed before they can so much as harm a wayward child. That wayward child is chased, even wounded, to the edge of the village for having gone into the forbidden parts of the forrest...but he survived, when he might otherwise have been slain. And those things which the Monster tacitly forbids? All are things which endanger those who do them, endanger the town as a whole if ignored, or are otherwise harmful.<br /> <br /> The Lunar is a horrifying beast and predator that everybody in town is afraid of. A force of nature that they all are only partially comfortable with, and then only because they have the taboos figured out. But it keeps them safe, gives them room to prosper and grow, while other villages without such a terrorizing beast have floundered and even been wiped out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:32:02-08:00","id":779026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778684#post778684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ................. why did I read that in Rarity's voice?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wasn't thinking of her specifically, she's definitely the archetype I was going for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:46:46-08:00","id":779194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/776169-exalted-fans-have-contradictory-desires-for-and-ideas-about-lunar-shapeshifting?p=778845#post778845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, my polyamory was an aside. You'll notice I didn't bring it up when I made my point, which was that the notion that people are trying to play &amp;quot;good people&amp;quot; seems at odds with the premise of the game; to me, if you come in with the intent of playing a shining knight all dressed in white (which I generally don't), it's for the sake of seeing what happens when he gets mud splattered all over his cuirass.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, i completely agree with you. Some of the players I've had don't, though, and I've witnessed players slut-shaming their own character despite the fact that they were the ones that made them for the purpose of &quot;using their wiles&quot; and whatnot. It was weird.<br /> <br /> Anyway, i'll stop talking about people who aren't there to defend themselves now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T17:35:23-08:00","id":779381,"title":"","content":"Personally, I dislike it when players try to play a (metaphorical) knight in shining armour... because I know that they'll make morally dubious choices (who doesn't! Morality is hard, especially when you're in a brutal bronze-age setting full of poverty, ignorance and strife) and then refuse to admit they're not the good guy and get upset with the other players when the other characters criticise their character's morality.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm glad the Virtues are gone. They were cool, but in my experience very few players roleplayed high virtues well. Especially multiple high virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}